      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "常见问题与故障排除",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**某个标签被跳过了。** 打开日志：跳过原因会按类别列出（体素数过少、空标签、没有可测量的路径、属于壳体或薄片）。报告的 Skipped 一节也会重复这些信息。"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**长度明显偏大。** 说明没有执行平滑，或平滑强度不足。请执行 **3 Smooth** 页，并观察 *Reduction* 百分比。"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**长度明显偏小。** 查看 *blunt ends* 提示与 **End radius**：在平齐端面处骨架会比实体短约一个局部半径（实测半径 2 时短 1 个体素，半径 6 时短 7 个）。该值**不会**被自动加到长度上，因为端面形状无法从掩模判断。"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**结果被标为 not elongated。** 该标签的长度与等效球直径之比小于 1，说明它不是细长物体，对它测量中心线长度没有意义。"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**出现 symmetry fallback 提示。** 该标签关于体素边界完全对称（例如截面恰为 4×4 的方柱，或圆心落在体素边界上的圆柱），细化算法会把它整体删除。插件对其做一次单体素膨胀后重新测量，因此结果可能有约一个体素的偏差。"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**菜单里找不到该插件。** Dragonfly 在启动时构建菜单，安装或启用之后必须**完全重启**。"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "注意事项与已知限制",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**只测量第 0 个时间点**。含多个时间点的 Multi-ROI 会在日志与报告中明确报出被忽略的时间点数量。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**带分枝的标签只报告主干长度**，侧枝被排除，排除比例见 Discarded 列——这是定义，不是误差。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**含环路的网络无法用单一长度描述**。插件仍会给出最长路径，但同时标出 *contains a loop*。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**端部缺失不会被自动补偿**（见常见问题）。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**平滑是可选的，但对弯曲对象强烈建议开启**；轴向或恰好 45° 的直线本身没有偏差，平滑对其完全没有影响。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "本插件**不会修改**原 Multi-ROI 的标签本身，只追加一个 scalar slot。"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "参考资料",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "T. C. Lee, R. L. Kashyap, C. N. Chu, *Building skeleton models via 3-D medial surface/axis thinning algorithms*, CVGIP: Graphical Models and Image Processing, 56(6):462–478, 1994 —— `skimage.morphology.skeletonize(method=\"lee\")` 所实现的算法。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "scikit-image、SciPy（`scipy.ndimage`、`scipy.sparse.csgraph`）官方文档。"},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "插件仓库内的 `DESIGN.md`：记录了本文所引用的全部实测数据与设计取舍。"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Starting from one published **Multi-ROI**, extracts a centerline for every non-zero label, measures its **real length**, and appends that length to the same Multi-ROI as a new **per-label scalar slot**. The five tabs are the workflow: **Input → Centerline → Smooth → Length measurement → Report**."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Unlike simply summing a skeleton polyline, this plugin **classifies the shape of each label before measuring it**: an open curve and a branched skeleton are measured along the longest weighted geodesic path; a **closed ring is measured as a ring**; a shell or plate has no centerline and is refused with a stated reason."},
        {"kind": "note", "text": "A digital skeleton staircases, so summing it directly reports a length that is **too large**. Measured: +9.0% on a shallow line, +10.5% on a 3-D diagonal, +21.7% at 5:1 anisotropy. The **Smooth** tab removes exactly that; at the default settings the same phantoms all measure to within roughly 1%."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Use cases",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Per-label length of **slender, curved** objects: vessels, fibres, channels, cracks."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Data whose voxel skeleton is visibly jagged, or whose Z spacing is much larger than X and Y (anisotropic)."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Workflows that need the length **written back onto the Multi-ROI** so labels can be coloured, filtered or exported by length."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Hundreds of labels at once: measured 0.32 s in total for 300 labels in a 120×300×300 volume (about 1.1 ms per label). Reading the Multi-ROI out of Dragonfly dominates the run."},
        {"kind": "note", "text": "**Not suitable** for solid blobs, shells or plates. Such labels have no meaningful length, and the plugin flags them *not elongated* or refuses them outright rather than printing a plausible wrong number."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Installation & enabling",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "steps", "steps": [
          "Run the Prototype Apps installer (Full Package / App Store package).",
          "Tick **Centerline and Length (v2)** in the plugin list.",
          "**Restart Dragonfly completely** — menus are built at startup, so a new entry does not appear until then.",
          "Open it from **Prototype Apps ▸ Measurements & Analysis ▸ Centerline and Length (v2)...**"
        ]},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Use the **Menu Item Manager** to hide the entry temporarily. Disabling only hides the menu; it does not remove the installed code directory."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Runtime environment & first-run setup",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "p", "text": "This is an `in_process` plugin: there is **no first-run setup at all**. No virtual environment, no model download, no internet, no GPU and no administrator access."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "It uses only the **PyQt6, NumPy, SciPy and scikit-image** bundled with Dragonfly. It is verified on Dragonfly 2025.1 (Python 3.10.13 / scikit-image 0.19.3) and 2027.1 (Python 3.14.3 / scikit-image 0.25.2), with bit-identical results."},
        {"kind": "note", "text": "The HTML report is a **self-contained local file**. Nothing is uploaded anywhere."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Interface",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "h3", "text": "1 Input"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Pick a published **MultiROI** and a **Time step**, then **Read input**. The **Optional steps** group configures the one-button run: *Include smoothing* and *Include report* are ticked by default, *Publish extracted centerlines* and *Publish smoothed centerlines* are not. **Execute all steps with current settings** runs the whole pipeline."},
        {"kind": "h3", "text": "2 Centerline"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Set **Minimum label size (voxels)** and press **Extract centerlines**. **Publish centerlines** publishes the result as a Dragonfly Graph carrying a Label ID scalar."},
        {"kind": "h3", "text": "3 Smooth (optional)"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**Iterations**, **Smoothing factor** and **Resampling step (voxels)** control the strength; press **Smooth centerlines**. This step can be skipped entirely."},
        {"kind": "h3", "text": "4 Length measurement"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**Measure from** selects raw or smoothed centerlines and **Scalar slot name** names the slot. **Measure lengths** fills the table and **Write as new MultiROI scalar slot** writes it back. Beside the lengths the table gives **Shape, Discarded, Length / diameter and Warnings**; hovering a row explains what each warning costs for that label."},
        {"kind": "h3", "text": "5 Report (optional)"},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "Choose an output path and press **Generate report** to write a self-contained local HTML file."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "steps", "steps": [
          "On **1 Input**, choose the Multi-ROI and time step, then **Read input**.",
          "On **2 Centerline**, set the minimum label size and press **Extract centerlines**; read the log for labels that were skipped and why.",
          "(Optional) On **3 Smooth**, press **Smooth centerlines** to remove the staircase bias.",
          "On **4 Length measurement**, choose the source and press **Measure lengths**; check the Shape and Warnings columns.",
          "Press **Write as new MultiROI scalar slot** to store the lengths on the Multi-ROI.",
          "(Optional) On **5 Report**, generate the HTML report."
        ]},
        {"kind": "note", "text": "All of the above can be done in one click with **Execute all steps with current settings** on **1 Input**; the two checkboxes there decide whether Smooth and Report take part."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Parameters",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "table", "table": {
          "headers": ["Parameter", "Default", "Range", "Meaning"],
          "rows": [
            ["Time step", "0", "0–9999", "Which time step to read. A Multi-ROI with several time steps is measured one step at a time, and the number ignored is stated in the log rather than dropped silently."],
            ["Minimum label size (voxels)", "8", "2–100000000", "Labels smaller than this are skipped and listed under Skipped."],
            ["Iterations", "12", "0–500", "Laplacian smoothing iterations. 0 means no smoothing."],
            ["Smoothing factor", "0.35", "0.00–1.00", "How far each point moves towards the mean of its neighbours per iteration. Larger is stronger."],
            ["Resampling step (voxels)", "1.00", "0.10–20.00", "The polyline is resampled to this step before smoothing. It is multiplied by the **smallest voxel spacing** internally, so the same setting is the same physical window on anisotropic data."],
            ["Measure from", "Smoothed", "Raw / Smoothed", "Which set of centerlines the length is taken from. Only Raw is available if smoothing was not run."],
            ["Scalar slot name", "Centerline Length (v2)", "any text", "Name of the scalar slot written back. An existing slot of the same name is updated rather than duplicated."]
          ]}},
        {"kind": "note", "text": "**Too many iterations, or too large a factor, keep shortening the path** past the point where only the staircase is being removed. Compare *Raw length* with *Measured length* and read *Reduction*: sensible smoothing takes 1%–10% off, not tens of percent."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Output",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**A new scalar slot on the Multi-ROI**: per-label length in metres, carrying a length dimension, usable directly for colouring or filtering by length."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**The lengths table**: Label, Name, Voxels, Points, Raw length, Measured length, Reduction, Shape, Discarded, Length / diameter, Warnings."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**Dragonfly Graphs** (optional): raw and smoothed centerlines, each carrying a Label ID scalar, viewable in the 3-D scene."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**An HTML report** (optional): one self-contained file with the full table, the run settings, the skipped labels, and a legend for exactly those warnings that actually occurred."},
        {"kind": "table", "table": {
          "headers": ["Shape", "Meaning", "How it is measured"],
          "rows": [
            ["Open curve", "a simple open curve", "longest weighted geodesic path"],
            ["Branched", "a tree with side branches", "longest weighted geodesic path; branches are excluded and the excluded fraction is given under Discarded"],
            ["Closed loop", "a closed ring", "as a ring; measured as an open path it would read about half"],
            ["Network", "a skeleton containing loops", "longest weighted geodesic path; one length cannot describe the whole structure"],
            ["Surface", "a shell or plate", "refused"],
            ["Single point / No skeleton", "a degenerate skeleton", "refused"]
          ]}}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "FAQ & troubleshooting",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**A label was skipped.** Read the log: the reasons are grouped (too few voxels, empty label, no measurable path, shell or plate). The Skipped section of the report repeats them."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**The length looks too large.** Smoothing was not run, or was too weak. Run the **3 Smooth** tab and watch the *Reduction* percentage."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**The length looks too small.** Look for the *blunt ends* warning and the **End radius** column: at a flat end the skeleton stops short by roughly the local radius (measured: 1 voxel at r=2, 7 voxels at r=6). It is **not** added to the length, because the cap shape that would decide the true figure cannot be known from the mask."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**A result is flagged *not elongated*.** That label's length divided by its equivalent sphere diameter is below 1, so it is not a slender object and a centerline length is not meaningful for it."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**A result is flagged *symmetry fallback*.** That label is perfectly symmetric about a voxel boundary (for example a prism of exactly 4×4 cross-section, or a cylinder centred on a voxel boundary), and thinning deletes such a body entirely. The plugin re-measures it after a one-voxel dilation, so expect about one voxel of deviation."},
        {"kind": "p", "text": "**The plugin is not in the menu.** Dragonfly builds its menus at startup; **restart it completely** after installing or enabling."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Notes & known limitations",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**Only time step 0 is measured.** A Multi-ROI with more time steps reports how many were ignored, in the log and in the report."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**A branched label reports its trunk only.** Side branches are excluded and the excluded fraction is in the Discarded column — that is the definition, not an error."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**A network with loops cannot be described by one length.** The longest path is still given, flagged *contains a loop*."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**End shortening is never compensated automatically** (see the FAQ)."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**Smoothing is optional but strongly recommended for curved objects.** An axis-aligned or exactly-45° line is unbiased to begin with, and smoothing leaves it completely unchanged."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "The plugin **never modifies the labels** of the source Multi-ROI; it only appends a scalar slot."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "References",
      "blocks": [
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "T. C. Lee, R. L. Kashyap, C. N. Chu, *Building skeleton models via 3-D medial surface/axis thinning algorithms*, CVGIP: Graphical Models and Image Processing, 56(6):462–478, 1994 — the algorithm behind `skimage.morphology.skeletonize(method=\"lee\")`."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "scikit-image and SciPy documentation (`scipy.ndimage`, `scipy.sparse.csgraph`)."},
        {"kind": "bullet", "text": "`DESIGN.md` in the plugin repository: every measurement quoted in this manual, with the phantom it was taken from."}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "CGAL Mesh_3 (Panel)",
  "cn": {
    "func": "将您的分割结果转换为可直接用于仿真的四面体（体）网格。在面板中选择一个 Multi-ROI、二值 ROI 或标签图像，设置网格质量参数（面角度/尺寸/距离、单元尺寸——均为真实世界单位），点击 Generate Mesh：插件即生成位于 Dragonfly 真实世界坐标系中的 .vtu（可选 .mesh）文件，每个四面体都带有原始材料/标签编号，可直接在 ParaView 或仿真软件中打开。",
    "scenarios": "适用于需要在分割后的三维图像数据上进行物理仿真（有限元应力、传热、流体、电磁等）的用户——例如铸件或增材制造零件的工业 CT、材料科学中的电池电极和多孔材料、生命科学中的骨骼与组织结构。多材料网格化会将每个分割相保留为网格中的独立材料。",
    "requirements": "首次使用需一次性构建随附的 CGAL 网格生成程序（面板中的 Setup Environment 按钮）；构建过程需要联网；无需 GPU。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Turns your segmentation into a simulation-ready tetrahedral (volume) mesh. Select a Multi-ROI, a binary ROI, or a label image in the panel, set the mesh quality criteria (facet angle/size/distance, cell size — in real-world units), and click Generate Mesh: the plugin produces a .vtu (and optional .mesh) file in true Dragonfly world coordinates, with each tetrahedron tagged by its original material/label, ready to open in ParaView or a simulation package.",
    "scenarios": "For anyone who needs to run physics simulations (FEM stress, heat transfer, fluid flow, electromagnetics) on segmented 3D image data — e.g. industrial CT of cast or additively manufactured parts, battery electrodes and porous materials in materials science, or bone and tissue structures in life science. Multi-material meshing preserves each segmented phase as a separate material in the mesh.",
    "requirements": "First use requires a one-time build of the bundled CGAL mesher program (Setup Environment button in the panel); needs internet for the build; no GPU required."
  }
}

{
  "title": "Train/Infer Cellpose on Cloud Server",
  "cn": {
    "func": "该插件把 Cellpose 模型的训练与推理都放到云端服务器的免费 GPU 上完成，界面采用与内置 Cellpose 插件一致的\"训练（左）| 推理（右）\"双栏布局，并在顶部提供一个\"云服务器\"下拉框，可选择五个平台之一：Google Colab、Kaggle、百度飞桨 AI Studio、阿里 ModelScope 魔搭，以及 Remote Dragonfly Server（远程 Dragonfly 服务器）。适用于本机没有独立显卡（或显存太小、跑不动 Cellpose-SAM）的情况。工作方式：插件在进程内读取 Dragonfly 数据（训练用图像通道 + MultiROI，或推理用图像通道 + 本地模型），打包后交给所选云平台的 GPU 运行，训练得到的模型下载回本地保存，推理得到的掩膜则作为 MultiROI 发布回 Dragonfly。前四个 notebook 平台都支持\"手动\"模式：插件把数据包和对应的 notebook 导出到本地，您在浏览器里上传运行、下载 output.zip，再用\"载入模型/载入结果\"按钮导回——无需任何账号 API 或环境配置。其中 Google Colab 与 Kaggle 还支持\"自动\"模式：Colab 通过 Google Drive、Kaggle 通过其数据集+内核 API（完全无需浏览器点击）自动上传数据、运行、回传结果；自动模式需一次性提供对应凭据（Colab 用 Google 的 client_secret.json 或 service_account.json；Kaggle 用 kaggle.json），并一次性点击\"设置云端传输\"（用 Dragonfly 自带 Python 建一个只含 Google Drive 与 Kaggle 客户端的小型虚拟环境，不含 torch）。AI Studio 与 ModelScope 因缺少稳定的公开无头运行接口，仅提供手动模式。第五个选项 Remote Dragonfly Server 则是连接到另一台（或本机）通过 Prototype Apps ▸ Server Management 启动了 Prototype Labs TCP 服务器的 Dragonfly：插件用 IP/端口/令牌连上后，把数据上传到服务器、在服务器自带的 Dragonfly Python（已内置 cellpose+torch，用它的 GPU）上训练/推理，再把模型/结果下载回来——无需 notebook、无需 venv、无需 pip，也无需任何云账号或翻墙，仅支持自动模式。",
    "scenarios": "适用于没有 NVIDIA 显卡、或显存不足以训练 Cellpose-SAM 的电脑，希望借助各类云平台的免费 GPU 训练/微调并应用细胞、细胞核等分割模型的场景。国内用户在 Colab 被墙或过慢时，可切换到国内可直连的百度飞桨 AI Studio 或阿里 ModelScope（手动模式），或使用团队内一台带好显卡的机器作为 Remote Dragonfly Server。也适合先在云端训练自定义模型、再在云端把它应用到整套数据的工作流。",
    "requirements": "前四个 notebook 平台需要相应账号（Colab / Kaggle / AI Studio / ModelScope）与网络连接；本机无需独立显卡（GPU 由云平台/远程服务器提供）。自动模式（Colab / Kaggle）还需对应的凭据文件；手动模式（前四个平台）无需任何 API 或环境配置；Remote Dragonfly Server 只需远程服务器的 IP/端口/令牌（在那台机器上用 Prototype Apps ▸ Server Management 启动），无需任何云账号或翻墙。各免费额度有上限且会变动（如 Kaggle 每周约 30 GPU 小时、Colab 单次时长限制、AI Studio 每日算力点），超大训练可能需要付费档位。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "This plugin runs both Cellpose training and inference on a cloud server's free GPU. The UI uses the same Train (left) | Infer (right) two-column layout as the built-in Cellpose plugin, plus a Cloud server dropdown at the top that selects one of five hosts: Google Colab, Kaggle, Baidu PaddlePaddle AI Studio, Alibaba ModelScope, or a Remote Dragonfly Server. Use it when the PC has no discrete GPU (or one too small for Cellpose-SAM). How it works: the plugin reads your Dragonfly data in-process (an image Channel + MultiROI for training, or an image Channel + a local model for inference), packages it, runs the GPU work on the chosen host, then downloads the trained model to a local folder or publishes the inferred masks back as a MultiROI. The four notebook hosts support a Manual mode: the plugin exports a data package plus a host-tailored notebook, you upload/run/download output.zip in the browser, then load it back with the Load model / Load result buttons - no account API or setup. Google Colab and Kaggle additionally support an Auto mode: Colab moves data via Google Drive and Kaggle via its datasets+kernels API (fully headless, no browser click), uploading, running and returning the result automatically; Auto needs a one-time credentials file (Colab: a Google client_secret.json or service_account.json; Kaggle: kaggle.json) and a one-time Setup Cloud Transfer that builds a tiny venv from Dragonfly's own Python (Google Drive + Kaggle clients only, no torch). AI Studio and ModelScope are Manual-only because they lack a clean public headless-run API. The fifth option, Remote Dragonfly Server, connects (by IP/port/token) to another machine - or this one - running the Prototype Labs TCP server inside Dragonfly (started via Prototype Apps > Server Management): the plugin uploads the data, runs Cellpose on the server's own Dragonfly Python (cellpose + torch already bundled, using its GPU) and downloads the model/result back - no notebook, no venv, no pip, and no cloud account or VPN; Auto-only.",
    "scenarios": "Ideal when the workstation has no NVIDIA GPU, or one too small to train Cellpose-SAM, and you want to use a cloud platform's free GPU to fine-tune and apply cell/nucleus segmentation models. Users in regions where Colab is blocked or slow can switch to the domestically reachable Baidu AI Studio or Alibaba ModelScope (Manual mode), or point the plugin at a team GPU box running as a Remote Dragonfly Server. It also fits a train-in-the-cloud then apply-in-the-cloud workflow.",
    "requirements": "The four notebook hosts need the matching account (Colab / Kaggle / AI Studio / ModelScope) and internet; no discrete GPU is required locally (the cloud host / remote server provides it). Auto mode (Colab / Kaggle) additionally needs the matching credentials file; Manual mode (the four notebook hosts) needs no API or environment setup; the Remote Dragonfly Server only needs the remote server's IP/port/token (started on that machine via Prototype Apps > Server Management), with no cloud account or VPN. Free tiers cap usage and change (e.g. Kaggle ~30 GPU-hours/week, Colab session limits, AI Studio daily compute points); very large trainings may need a paid tier."
  }
}

{
  "title_en": "Train/Infer Cellpose on Cloud Server",
  "title_cn": "在云端服务器上训练/推理 Cellpose 模型",
  "menu_en": "Train/Infer Cellpose on Cloud Server...",
  "version": "1.4",
  "date": "2026-07-19",
  "cn": [
    {
      "heading": "简介",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "本插件把 **Cellpose** 模型的**训练**与**推理**放到**云端服务器的免费 GPU** 上完成,界面采用与内置 Cellpose 插件一致的**训练(左)| 推理(右)双栏**布局,并在顶部提供一个 **Cloud server(云服务器)下拉框**。适用于本机没有独立显卡、或显存太小跑不动 Cellpose-SAM 的情况——本机只负责读取数据与发布结果,真正耗费显卡的计算在云端完成。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "为什么需要在浏览器点一下:免费版云 notebook 没有公开的\"无头运行\"接口,GPU 计算必须在浏览器标签页里点 Run all。插件会自动生成好 notebook,并把其余环节(读数据、打包、传输、发布)都自动化。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "云服务器与模式",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "顶部下拉框选择五个平台之一,并选择 **Auto(自动)** 或 **Manual(手动)** 模式:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "云服务器 / Host",
              "自动 Auto",
              "手动 Manual",
              "凭据 / Credentials"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Google Colab",
                "✅",
                "✅",
                "OAuth client_secret.json 或 service_account.json"
              ],
              [
                "Kaggle",
                "✅",
                "✅",
                "kaggle.json 文件,或 KGAT_ 令牌 + 用户名"
              ],
              [
                "百度飞桨 AI Studio",
                "—",
                "✅",
                "无(手动)"
              ],
              [
                "阿里 ModelScope 魔搭",
                "—",
                "✅",
                "无(手动)"
              ],
              [
                "Remote Dragonfly Server (via Prototype Apps)",
                "✅",
                "—",
                "服务器 IP + 端口(+ 令牌 token)"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**手动模式(前四家云 notebook 支持)**:插件把 input.zip 和对应平台的 notebook 导出到本地;你在浏览器里上传运行、下载 output.zip,再用\"载入模型/载入结果\"按钮导回。**无需任何账号 API 或环境配置。**"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**自动模式(Colab、Kaggle 与 Remote Dragonfly Server)**:插件自动上传数据、执行计算、并下载结果。Colab/Kaggle 需要一次性配置账号凭据(见下一节);Remote Dragonfly Server 只需填服务器 IP/端口/令牌(见\"远程 Dragonfly 服务器\"一节)。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Remote Dragonfly Server(远程 Dragonfly 服务器)**:连接到另一台(或本机)运行着 Prototype Labs TCP 服务器的 Dragonfly,把训练/推理放到**那台机器的 GPU** 上跑。它用服务器自带的 Dragonfly Python(已内置 cellpose+torch),**无需 notebook、无需 venv、无需 pip 安装**,也**不需要 Google/Kaggle 账号或翻墙**。仅支持自动模式。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "账号与凭据设置(自动模式必读)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**手动模式无需任何凭据,可跳过本节。** 自动模式(Colab / Kaggle)需要按下面一次性设置好账号、API 令牌与权限。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "Google Colab(自动)——OAuth 设置"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
