{
  "title": "Contact Area Analysis",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：分析已做好标签（labels）的 MultiROI 中每个标签与其它标签的接触情况：每对标签的接触面积、每个标签的接触总面积与配位数（接触伙伴数量）、表面积与接触占比，以及全部接触结果的统计汇总（均值/标准差/中位数/最大最小值等）。全部数值保存为一个 **.xlsx** 文件（Settings / Per-label / Pairs / Matrix / Statistics 五个工作表），并基于同一结果生成 **.docx 报告**（总览、统计表、直方图图表、Top 表格）。**接触的定义由用户选择**：（1）**面接触**——仅体素共享面计为接触，接触面积为共享面面积的精确总和；（2）**邻近接触**——考虑到分辨率、体素尺寸与分割精度造成的微小间隙，两标签体素**中心距离 ≤ 阈值**（默认 2 个体素步长，可改数值或改用 µm）即计为接触；此时接触面积按穿越间隙带（到两标签距离之和 ≤ 阈值的未标记体素）的网格线计数——平整间隙精确，曲面/阶梯间隙为保守下界；阈值取 1 时与面接触模式完全一致，两种模式可直接对比。纯棱/点接触（中心距 √2、√3）面积为 0，但仍列入接触对并给出最小中心距。本插件不创建、不修改会话中的任何对象。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：颗粒/晶粒材料中晶粒间接触面积与配位数分析（烧结、电池电极、岩土颗粒堆积）；多相分割后各相界面面积统计；细胞/器官分割中相邻结构的接触定量；需要把接触结果整理成 Excel 数据和 Word 报告直接交付的场合。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需安装、联网、GPU 或虚拟环境——进程内 PyQt6 + numpy + scipy + openpyxl + matplotlib（均为 Dragonfly 自带）。需要会话中有已发布、已做标签的 MultiROI；体素尺寸无法读取时拒绝分析（面积将无意义）。邻近接触模式在各向异性体素 + 体素步长单位时会给出明确警告（各轴物理容差不同），可切换为 µm 单位阈值。数千标签规模可用：接触对按包围盒预筛，逐对在小包围盒内精确计算。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: analyzes how every label of a labelled MultiROI touches the other labels: contact area per label pair, per-label totals and coordination numbers (contact partner counts), surface areas and contact fractions, plus summary statistics (mean/std/median/min/max). Every number is saved into ONE .xlsx workbook (Settings / Per-label / Pairs / Matrix / Statistics sheets) and a .docx report is generated from the same results (overview, statistics, histograms, top tables). THE CONTACT DEFINITION IS THE USER'S CHOICE: (1) FACE CONTACT - only voxels sharing a face count, and the contact area is the exact sum of the shared faces' areas; (2) PROXIMITY - to tolerate the small gaps that resolution, voxel size and segmentation precision leave between bodies that physically touch, two labels whose voxel CENTRES lie within a threshold (default 2 voxel steps; value editable, or switch to um) count as contact; the area then counts grid lines crossing the true gap band (unlabelled voxels whose distances to the two labels sum to <= the threshold) - exact for flat gaps, a conservative lower bound on curved/staircase ones - and at threshold 1 this is EXACTLY face mode, so the two definitions are directly comparable. Pure edge/corner contacts (centre distance sqrt(2), sqrt(3)) have zero area but are still listed with their minimum centre distance. The plugin creates and modifies nothing in the session.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: grain-to-grain contact area and coordination-number analysis in granular/polycrystalline materials (sintering, battery electrodes, soil packing); interface-area statistics between phases after multi-phase segmentation; contact quantification between adjacent segmented structures in biology; any case where the contact results must land as an Excel workbook and a Word report ready to hand over.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no internet, no GPU, no venv - in-process PyQt6 + numpy + scipy + openpyxl + matplotlib (all bundled with Dragonfly). Needs a published, labelled MultiROI in the session; the analysis is REFUSED when the voxel size cannot be read (areas would be meaningless). Proximity mode warns explicitly on anisotropic voxels with a voxel-step threshold (the physical tolerance differs per axis) - switch the threshold to um instead. Scales to thousands of labels: candidate pairs are prefiltered by bounding box and each pair is computed exactly inside its own small box."
  }
}

{
  "title_en": "Contact Area Analysis",
  "title_cn": "Contact Area Analysis（标签接触面积分析）",
  "menu_en": "Analyze Contact Areas Between Labels...",
  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-09-01",
  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Analyzes how every label of a **labelled MultiROI** touches the other labels: the contact area of each label pair, each label's total contact area and coordination number (how many partners it touches), surface area and contact fraction, and summary statistics over all contacts."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Everything is saved into **one .xlsx workbook** (sheets: Settings, Per-label, Pairs, Matrix, Statistics) and, optionally, a **.docx report** built from the same results — overview, statistics, histograms and top tables."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "**Nothing is created or modified in the session.** The plugin reads the selected MultiROI and writes files where you point it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The two contact definitions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Face contact** — only voxels sharing a FACE count as contact; the contact area is the exact sum of the shared faces' areas (a voxelized interface, no estimate)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Proximity** — resolution, voxel size and segmentation precision can leave a thin gap between bodies that physically touch. In this mode two labels count as in contact when any two of their voxel **centres** lie within the threshold (default **2 voxel steps**; editable, or switch the unit to µm). The criterion is computed exactly, per pair, from Euclidean distance transforms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The proximity contact **area** is a grid-line crossing count over the true gap band: unlabelled voxels whose distances to the two labels sum to ≤ the threshold form a lens between the bodies, and along every grid line, each place where a run of label i and a run of label j touch directly or are separated only by lens voxels contributes one face. Flat gaps are counted exactly; staircase/curved gap columns join the area only once the lens bridges them along a grid line, so those areas are a conservative lower bound, and areas measured at different thresholds are not comparable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "At threshold 1 the proximity mode equals face mode EXACTLY, so results under the two definitions are directly comparable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "A pure edge/corner touch (centre distance √2 or √3) is a line/point contact: it is listed as a contact pair with its minimum centre distance, but its area is 0 — the geometric truth, stated rather than hidden."
        },
        {
          "kind": "warn",
          "text": "With anisotropic voxels and a threshold in voxel steps, the physical tolerance differs per axis; the result carries an explicit warning. Switch the threshold unit to µm for an isotropic physical tolerance."
        }
