          "text": "It is, however, an ordinary Qt menu living in the same process as this plugin, so an entry can simply be added to it. Two measured details decide how: Dragonfly creates a **new** menu object for every right-click and keeps the old ones, and it does **not** emit Qt's `aboutToShow` on them. So the plugin notices each menu as it is created and adds the entry then — which is why an entry appears without a restart, and why a menu Dragonfly rebuilds gets the entry straight back."
