          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**联接仅适用于同机各 NTFS 盘之间。** 网络盘/可移动盘不支持目录联接,请改用 Move 模式。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**版本兼容性**:2026.1 与 2027.1 视为同一格式(仅改名),互相兼容。当所选模型的来源版本与目标版本不同(且不属于此等价关系)时,会弹出兼容性警告让你确认是否继续。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "查看训练图像与可视化反馈",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "在表格里**右键**某个模型,选择 **Review Training Images and Visual Feedback(查看训练图像与可视化反馈)**,即可浏览该模型训练过程中保存的可视化反馈快照(模型文件夹内的 `visual_feedback_*.ORSObject` 文件)。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "查看器以**灰度显示输入图像**,并叠加各类别的**彩色分割(预测标签)**,提供:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**快照选择器**:按时间戳在训练过程中保存的多个快照之间切换(下拉框 + ◀ 上一个 / 下一个 ▶)。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**叠加层控制**:选择要显示的预测层,并可勾选/取消「显示叠加」。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**预测切片滑块**:对三维预测逐切片浏览。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**不透明度滑块**:调节分割叠加层的透明度;底部有类别颜色图例。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Save PNG…**:把当前视图另存为 PNG 图片。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "右键菜单还提供 **Open notes…**(打开/编辑该模型的备注)与 **Open model folder**(在资源管理器中打开模型的真实文件夹)。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "环境需求与注意事项",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**纯进程内运行**:无需 venv、无需联网、无需 GPU、无需管理员权限(目录联接 mklink /J 不需要管理员)。安装后**重启 Dragonfly** 即可在菜单中看到。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**仅 Windows / 同机 NTFS**:联接只在本机各 NTFS 盘之间有效;网络盘、可移动盘请使用 Move 模式。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**安全保护**:删除类操作(移除库中已有的重复真实拷贝)有二次确认;卸载联接时只用 `os.rmdir` 删除联接点本身,**绝不会**顺着联接把库里的真实文件误删。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**备注随模型迁移**:`notes.md` 保存在模型的真实文件夹内(联接会解析到其目标),因此备注始终跟随那一份库副本移动。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "本功能由第三方(Prototype Labs / Prototype Apps)提供,并非 Dragonfly 官方开发,Dragonfly 也不提供技术支持;使用风险由使用者自行承担。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**DL Model Organizer** manages the deep-learning segmentation models trained by Dragonfly's **DeepTrainer** from one central library: move them off C: to any drive with space, temporarily **attach** them back to a given Dragonfly version for training/inference, then free C: again — while keeping a **single copy** shared across versions on demand."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Background: DeepTrainer stores each model as a folder (`model.ORSModel` + `data.json` + checkpoints) in a fixed per-version C: directory, `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\comet\\Dragonfly<ver>\\pythonUserExtensions\\PythonPluginExtensions\\DeepTrainer\\models\\`. There is no built-in setting to relocate it, so C: fills up (tens of GB per version in practice) and every Dragonfly version keeps its own duplicate. This plugin exists to fix exactly those two problems."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "Use it to: reclaim C: when DeepTrainer models fill it; share one set of trained models across multiple Dragonfly versions (e.g. 2025.1 and 2027.1) without duplicating them; and attach the models you need to the current version for a training/inference session, then free the space afterwards."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Features",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Central model library**: set one library root (e.g. `D:\\DragonflyModels`); the path is persisted and remembered next time."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Cross-version table**: scans every Dragonfly version on C: plus the library, one row per model, showing name, origin version (read from `data.json`'s `dragonflyVersion`), size, whether it is in the library, last-modified time, and which versions it is present in."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Move to Library**: move a version's C: model into the library, freeing C: immediately."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Attach →**: place a library model into a chosen **target version**. By default this uses a **Windows directory junction (mklink /J)** — no admin, instant, ~0 C: usage, one shared copy kept in the library; or switch to **Move** to physically relocate the single copy into that version."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Detach**: remove a model from a version. A junction is just unlinked and the library copy is untouched; a real folder that was move-attached is moved back to the library; a redundant real duplicate already in the library can be deleted after confirmation."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Live refresh, no restart**: after attach/detach the CURRENTLY running version's model list is auto-refreshed (`refreshModelsList`), so the change shows in AI/DeepTrainer without a restart (other versions pick it up on next launch)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Batch actions**: the table supports Ctrl/Shift multi-select and Ctrl+A select-all; Move to Library / Attach / Detach act on every selected row, and each confirmation (version mismatch, deleting duplicates) is asked once for the whole batch."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Search, notes, visual feedback**: a search box filters by name/ID/version/location; every row has a **Notes** button editing a `notes.md` that travels with the model; right-clicking a model opens a **training-image visual-feedback viewer** (see below)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Space hints**: the bottom line shows the library's free space (GB) and each version's reclaimable size."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "Open **Prototype Apps ▸ Train Custom Model ▸ DL Model Organizer...** to bring up the dockable panel.",
            "On the **Central model library** row, click **Browse…** and pick a folder on a drive with space (e.g. `D:\\DragonflyModels`), or paste the path. It is remembered.",
            "In the table, Ctrl/Shift-click one or more models (Ctrl+A selects all); the right-hand columns show which versions each model lives in, its size, and whether it is in the library.",
            "**Free C:** — select a version's C: model and click **Move to Library**; the files are moved into the library and C: is freed immediately.",
            "**Attach back to a version** — pick the **Target version** in the dropdown, choose an **Attach mode** (Junction by default, or Move), select a library model, and click **Attach →**. The default junction completes instantly with ~0 C: usage.",
            "**Free the space when done** — select a model no longer needed in a version and click **Detach**; a junction is just unlinked, and the library copy stays.",
            "After attach/detach, the running version's model list auto-refreshes — the model is usable in AI / DeepTrainer with no Dragonfly restart."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "The log pane at the bottom records each move/attach/detach action and its result; the status line reports how many succeeded and how many failed (failures detailed in the log)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Attach modes compared",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Attach** offers two modes, chosen with the radio buttons on the panel:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Mode",
              "How it works",
              "C: usage",
              "Copies",
              "On Detach"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Junction (default)",
                "creates a Windows directory junction (mklink /J, no admin, instant) in the version folder pointing at the one library copy",
                "~0",
                "one shared copy",
                "removes only the junction; library copy untouched"
              ],
              [
                "Move (physical)",
                "physically relocates the single copy from the library into the version folder",
                "the full model size",
                "still one (relocated)",
                "moves the folder back to the library"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Junctions work between local NTFS drives on the same machine only.** Network/removable drives do not support them — use Move mode there."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Version compatibility**: 2026.1 and 2027.1 are treated as the same format (a rename) and are compatible. Attaching a model whose origin version differs from the target (outside that equivalence) raises a compatibility warning to confirm before proceeding."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Review Training Images and Visual Feedback",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Right-click** a model in the table and choose **Review Training Images and Visual Feedback** to browse the visual-feedback snapshots saved during that model's training (the `visual_feedback_*.ORSObject` files inside the model folder)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The viewer shows the **input image in grayscale** with the per-class **predicted segmentation** overlaid, and provides:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Snapshot selector**: switch between the snapshots saved at different timestamps during training (a dropdown plus ◀ Prev / Next ▶)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Overlay control**: pick which prediction layer to show, and toggle \"Show overlay\" on/off."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Prediction-slice slider**: scrub slice by slice through a 3D prediction."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Opacity slider**: adjust the segmentation overlay's transparency; a class-color legend sits below the image."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Save PNG…**: save the current view as a PNG image."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "The right-click menu also offers **Open notes…** (open/edit the model's notes) and **Open model folder** (reveal the model's real folder in Explorer)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Requirements & notes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Runs purely in-process**: no venv, no internet, no GPU, and no admin rights (directory junctions via mklink /J need no admin). After installing, **restart Dragonfly** to see the menu item."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Windows / same-machine NTFS only**: junctions only work between local NTFS drives; use Move mode for network or removable drives."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Safety**: destructive actions (deleting a redundant real duplicate already in the library) require confirmation; detaching a junction uses `os.rmdir` on the reparse point only, so it can **never** follow the link and delete the library's real files."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Notes travel with the model**: `notes.md` lives inside the model's real folder (a junction is resolved to its target), so notes always follow the single library copy."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "This feature is provided by a third party (Prototype Labs / Prototype Apps), not officially developed or supported by Dragonfly. Use at your own risk."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "View/Search Dragonfly Publications",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：一个轻量版 Obsidian，用于查看和搜索一批“使用了 Dragonfly 软件”的论文合集。这些论文以 Markdown 形式内置在插件里（从 All_Materials_Organized_by_AI 项目导出，按 Dragonfly 相关性筛选为 高+中 两档）。界面左侧是可搜索、**按学科分组**的论文树（带相关性徽标 🟢高/🟡中）+ 相关性筛选；右侧渲染论文内容，并可在 英文 / 中文 摘要 / 全文 三个版本间切换。搜索为全文子串匹配，支持任意语言（中文可直接搜），覆盖标题、作者、正文。纯查看器：读取内置 Markdown，用 Qt 原生渲染，不调用 Dragonfly 对象模型、无需联网/GPU/虚拟环境。将来只需在 All_Materials_Organized_by_AI 项目重新导出并重新打包本项目，即可更新论文合集，插件代码无需改动。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：快速浏览/检索“别人怎么用 Dragonfly 做研究”的论文案例；按主题（分割、CT、材料、古生物、生物医学等）全文搜索；给销售/市场/技术支持提供文献佐证；离线随插件一起分发的论文知识库。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需安装、无需联网、无需 GPU、无需虚拟环境。论文 Markdown 随插件一并打包（pub_viewer_code\\pubs），只包含约 91 篇筛选后的论文（约 6 MB），不含原始 PDF/视频。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: a lite-Obsidian viewer for browsing and searching a collection of publications that USED Dragonfly. The papers ship as markdown bundled inside the plugin (exported from the All_Materials_Organized_by_AI project, filtered to Dragonfly Relevance High+Medium). Left: a searchable tree of papers **grouped by discipline** with a relevance badge (🟢 High / 🟡 Medium) + a relevance filter. Right: the rendered paper with a switch between the English / 中文 summary and the full text. Search is full-text substring matching across title/authors/body and works in any language (Chinese searches directly). Pure viewer: it reads the bundled markdown with Qt's native renderer — no Dragonfly object-model use, no internet/GPU/venv. To update the collection, just re-export from All_Materials_Organized_by_AI and repackage this project; the plugin code never changes.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: quickly browse/search real examples of how others used Dragonfly in research; full-text search by topic (segmentation, CT, materials, palaeontology, biomedical, …); provide literature evidence for sales/marketing/support; an offline, bundled publication knowledge base.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no internet, no GPU, no venv. The publication markdown ships with the plugin (pub_viewer_code\\pubs) — only the ~91 filtered papers (~6 MB), never the original PDFs/videos."
  }
}

