    {"heading": "参考资料", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "CellProfiler 的 MeasureImageQuality / MeasureGranularity / MeasureObjectIntensityDistribution 模块文档（仅作为**需要测什么**的参考，本插件未使用其源码）：https://cellprofiler-manual.s3.amazonaws.com/CellProfiler-4.2.8/modules/measurement.html"},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Matheron, G.：粒度分析（granulometry）的数学形态学基础"},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "SciPy `ndimage` 形态学与滤波器文档"}
    ]}
  ],
  "en": [
    {"heading": "Introduction", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Before anything is measured, this plugin answers a more basic question: **is this acquisition good enough to measure?** It checks focus, saturation, noise and spectrum, reports the dominant structure scale, and examines how intensity is distributed inside each object."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "The panel is six numbered steps. Changing anything upstream invalidates the results below it, so an exported number always matches the settings on screen; long analyses run on a worker thread, and cancel or failure publishes nothing."},
      {"kind": "note", "text": "Voxel spacing is read from Dragonfly's geometry. **Anisotropic data is genuinely resampled** where a metric needs isotropy, instead of averaging the three spacings and calling the result a physical length — that number would not be a length."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Use cases", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Screen a batch of scans before analysis: catch out-of-focus, clipped or noisy data early."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Multi-channel imaging: check for bleed-through or misalignment via channel correlation."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Find the dominant particle or pore scale with 3D granulometry."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "See whether intensity inside an object is uniform or edge-loaded: shells, coatings, stain penetration depth."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Installation & enabling", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "steps", "steps": [
        "Install the Prototype Apps package (or tick this plugin in the App Store).",
        "The plugin is **disabled by default** — enable it in the App Store or the Menu Item Manager.",
        "**Restart Dragonfly completely** (plugins are discovered at startup only).",
        "Open it from Prototype Apps ▸ 3D Measurement & Acquisition QA… (group: Measurements & Analysis)."
      ]}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Runtime environment & first-run setup", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**Nothing to install or configure.** It runs entirely in Dragonfly's own Python using the NumPy and SciPy it already ships. No internet, no download, no GPU, no virtual environment."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "The **Environment** line reports what is available (channel publishing, MultiROI reading). Anything unavailable disables the matching feature and says why."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Interface", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "p", "text": "A fixed header shows the environment, the current input, the current task, a progress bar and **Cancel**."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "1. Setup & Data"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Pick a Channel (published objects only), optionally an ROI mask and a MultiROI, and a timestep. The shape, the three spacings, whether the data is anisotropic and the timestep count are shown, and the granulometry radius range is derived from the voxel size."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "2. Image Quality"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Focus (global plus the minimum, median and 5th percentile over blocks), saturation (low and high counted separately), intensity statistics, noise (MAD x 1.4826) and SNR, and the power-spectrum slope."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "3. Granularity"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Grey openings over a series of **physical** radii give the retained curve, the size spectrum and the peak radius. The radius range follows the voxel size, and a radius too large for the data is skipped with an explicit message rather than exhausting memory."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "4. Radial Distribution"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "For each MultiROI label, intensity fraction and mean over **equal-volume** concentric shells, plus the radial CV. Equal volume rather than equal thickness, otherwise the outermost shell always dominates simply by being bigger."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "5. Batch QC Rules"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Threshold rules applied to the step-2 metrics give pass / warn / fail with the triggering reason. A metric a rule names but the measurement does not provide is reported as **missing**, never as a pass."},
      {"kind": "h3", "text": "6. Results & Export"},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "Publish a focus or noise Channel (a new object inheriting the source geometry), or export CSV, JSON and a self-contained HTML report."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "How to use", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "steps", "steps": [
        "Step 1: choose the Channel (and an ROI mask / MultiROI if needed).",
        "Step 2: run image quality; read saturation and SNR first.",
        "Step 3: run granularity and read the peak radius.",
        "Step 4 (needs a MultiROI): run the radial distribution.",
        "Step 5: set thresholds and run the batch QC.",
        "Step 6: publish a map or export a report."
      ]}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Parameters", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "table", "table": {
        "headers": ["Parameter", "Default", "Range", "Meaning"],
        "rows": [
          ["Timestep", "0", "0…T−1", "Which frame of a multi-timestep dataset to analyse"],
          ["Max radius", "voxel x 8", "voxel … voxel x 32", "Largest structuring-element radius for granulometry, in physical units"],
          ["Radius step", "voxel", "voxel … x64", "Spacing between successive radii"],
          ["Resample to isotropic", "on", "on / off", "Resample anisotropic data first; with it off the result is not a physical length"],
          ["Shells per object", "8", "2…64", "Number of equal-volume shells for the radial distribution"],
          ["Intensity-weighted center", "on", "on / off", "Off uses the geometric centroid"],
          ["saturated fraction >", "0.01", "0…1", "Fail threshold for the clipped fraction"],
          ["SNR <", "3.0", "0…1000", "Fail threshold for signal-to-noise"]
        ]
      }}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Output", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**Focus / noise Channel**: a newly published Channel inheriting the source spacing and geometry. The source is never modified."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**CSV**: image-quality metrics, the granulometry curve, and per-label per-shell radial values."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**JSON**: the full structured result set."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "**HTML**: a self-contained report containing only the steps that actually ran."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "FAQ & troubleshooting", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**My channel is not listed.** Only **published** objects appear; publish it, then press Refresh in step 1."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**Granularity says radii were skipped.** In voxels those radii exceed the cap (32 voxels, and never more than half the shortest volume axis). Downsample first, or lower the maximum radius."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**The step-4 button is greyed out.** The radial distribution needs a MultiROI; select one in step 1."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**SNR is blank.** The noise estimate was zero (perfectly flat synthetic data, for instance), which makes SNR meaningless."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**The QC table shows 'missing'.** A rule names a metric this run did not measure; the plugin will not treat that as a pass."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "Notes & known limitations", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "This plugin does **not** compute Radiomics texture features (GLCM/GLRLM and friends) — the MultiROI Label Classifier owns those, and duplicating them would give one quantity two numbers."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "It does not do spatial-relationship analysis (the CPC plugin) or segmentation comparison (the MiC plugin)."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "The structuring element is capped at 32 voxels and at half the shortest volume axis; for larger structures, downsample first."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "The power-spectrum slope depends on field of view and windowing. It is meant for comparing scans **within one batch**, not as an absolute number across instruments."},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Saturation is judged against the storage dtype's range; float data has no intrinsic range, so the observed minimum and maximum are used."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "References", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "CellProfiler's MeasureImageQuality / MeasureGranularity / MeasureObjectIntensityDistribution module documentation, used only as a reference for **which quantities matter** — no source was used: https://cellprofiler-manual.s3.amazonaws.com/CellProfiler-4.2.8/modules/measurement.html"},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "Matheron, G. — the mathematical-morphology basis of granulometry"},
      {"kind": "bullet", "text": "SciPy `ndimage` morphology and filter documentation"}
    ]}
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Mesh Element Quality & Printability",
  "cn": {
    "func": "按求解器和 3D 打印机的标准检查一个已发布的表面网格（可选加载 .vtu/.vtk 体网格）。六个编号步骤依次完成：选择网格与分析配置；表面完整性（是否水密、边界边、非流形边、重复面、退化面、朝向一致性、自相交、Euler 示性数与亏格）；单元质量（长宽比、最小/最大角、condition、scaled Jacobian、skewness 等 Verdict 指标，四面体/六面体另含体积、二面角与反转单元检测）；可打印性（悬垂面积、构建尺寸、锐边、射线法壁厚、以及对候选打印朝向的确定性排名扫描）；按配置阈值列出不合格单元；最后把结果写回为网格标量槽、发布仅含问题单元的网格副本，并导出 CSV / VTP / 自包含 HTML 报告。所有指标与 VTK 的 vtkMeshQuality（Verdict 参考实现）逐值校验一致。\n\n第一个页签上的**一键执行全部步骤（按当前设置）**会无人值守地跑完流程：曲面 → 网格质量 → 可打印性，每一步都使用你按下按钮那一刻各自页签上显示的设置。有三个步骤是复选框且**默认全部关闭**：朝向扫描（最多要做 512 次完整的悬垂分析），以及两个发布步骤（它们会向会话写入对象）。所有页签始终可以打开和修改参数，以便在运行**之前**检查各项阈值与打印设置；某一步所需的输入尚不存在时，按下**它自己的按钮**会给出提示，说明缺的是哪一步。",
    "scenarios": "适用于：有限元前处理时确认网格没有反转单元或极端长宽比；增材制造前评估某个打印朝向的悬垂面积与最小壁厚，并让插件扫描出更优朝向；工业 CT 分割重建后检查网格是否水密、有无自相交，再送去仿真或打印；以及在把网格交给下游工具之前，用「问题单元副本」直观定位需要修复的位置。",
    "requirements": "无需任何安装或配置：完全运行在 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 中，使用其已附带的 VTK 9.4.2 与 trimesh。不联网、不下载、不需要 GPU、不创建虚拟环境。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Checks a published surface mesh (optionally plus a .vtu/.vtk volumetric grid) the way a solver or a 3D printer will, in six numbered steps: pick the mesh and an analysis profile; surface integrity (watertightness, boundary and non-manifold edges, duplicate and degenerate faces, orientation consistency, self-intersections, Euler characteristic and genus); element quality (Verdict metrics — aspect ratio, min/max angle, condition, scaled Jacobian, skewness, plus volume, dihedral angles and inverted-cell detection for tets and hexes); printability (overhang area, build dimensions, sharp edges, ray-cast wall thickness and a deterministic ranked sweep over candidate build orientations); a review list of the elements that fail the chosen profile; and finally publishing the results as mesh scalar slots and a failed-element mesh copy, plus CSV, VTP and a self-contained HTML report. Every metric is cross-checked value-by-value against VTK's vtkMeshQuality, the Verdict reference implementation.\n\n**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the first tab runs the workflow unattended - surface, mesh quality, printability - each step with whatever its own tab shows when you press it. Three steps are tick boxes and all three are OFF by default: the orientation sweep, because it runs up to 512 full overhang analyses, and the two publishing steps, because they write to the session. Every tab stays open so the thresholds and the print settings can be read and changed BEFORE the run; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses when you press ITS button and says which step is missing.",
    "scenarios": "Use it to confirm an FEM mesh has no inverted cells or extreme aspect ratios before solving; to evaluate overhang area and minimum wall thickness for a chosen build direction and let the plugin sweep for a better one; to verify a mesh reconstructed from industrial CT is watertight and free of self-intersections before simulation or printing; and to locate what needs repair by publishing a mesh copy that contains only the failing elements.",
    "requirements": "Nothing to install or configure: it runs entirely in Dragonfly's own Python using the VTK 9.4.2 and trimesh it already ships. No internet, no download, no GPU, no virtual environment."
  }
}

{
  "title_en": "Mesh Element Quality & Printability",
  "title_cn": "Mesh Element Quality & Printability（网格单元质量与可打印性）",
  "menu_en": "Mesh Element Quality & Printability...",
  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-08-01",
  "cn": [
    {
      "heading": "简介",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "本插件按**求解器**和**3D 打印机**的标准检查一个已发布的表面网格，并可选地一并检查从 `.vtu` / `.vtk` 文件加载的体网格。它不修改你的输入：所有结果要么写成网格的新标量槽，要么发布为新的网格对象。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "面板分为 6 个编号步骤，前一步完成后才会启用下一步；任何上游输入或参数变化都会使下游结果失效，因此导出的数字永远对应当前设置。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "所有单元质量指标遵循 **Verdict** 定义（VTK 的 `vtkMeshQuality` 即其参考实现），并由自动化测试逐值比对，保证与其他基于 Verdict 的工具可直接对照。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "第一个页签上的**一键执行全部步骤（按当前设置）**会无人值守地跑完流程：曲面 → 网格质量 → 可打印性，每一步都使用你按下按钮那一刻各自页签上显示的设置。有三个步骤是复选框且**默认全部关闭**：朝向扫描（最多要做 512 次完整的悬垂分析），以及两个发布步骤（它们会向会话写入对象）。所有页签始终可以打开和修改参数，以便在运行**之前**检查各项阈值与打印设置；某一步所需的输入尚不存在时，按下**它自己的按钮**会给出提示，说明缺的是哪一步。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "适用场景",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "有限元前处理：确认网格没有**反转单元**、没有极端长宽比或过小的最小角。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "增材制造：评估某个打印朝向的**悬垂面积**与**最小壁厚**，并让插件扫描出更优朝向。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "工业 CT 分割重建后：检查网格是否**水密**、有无**自相交**，再送去仿真或打印。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "定位修复位置：发布只包含不合格单元的网格副本，在 3D 视图中直接看到问题在哪。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "安装与启用",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "安装 Prototype Apps 完整包（或在 App Store 中勾选本插件）。",
            "本插件默认**未启用**，请在 App Store 或菜单项管理器中启用它。",
            "**完全重启 Dragonfly**（插件只在启动时被发现）。",
            "从菜单打开：Prototype Apps ▸ Mesh Element Quality & Printability…（分组：Simulation & Meshing）。"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "运行环境与首次配置",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**无需任何安装或配置。** 本插件完全运行在 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 进程内，使用其已附带的 VTK 9.4.2 与 trimesh。不联网、不下载、不需要 GPU、不创建虚拟环境。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "面板顶部的 **Environment** 一行会实时显示三项能力：VTK 版本、标量写回是否可用、壁厚计算是否可用（依赖 trimesh）。若某项显示不可用，相关功能会被禁用并说明原因，而不会给出错误结果。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "界面说明",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "面板顶部固定显示：运行环境、当前输入、当前任务、进度条与 **Cancel** 按钮。长时间计算在工作线程中进行，界面不会卡死；取消或失败都**不会**发布任何半成品。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "1. 环境与输入"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "选择一个**已发布**的网格（列表只显示已发布对象），可选填一个 `.vtu` / `.vtk` 体网格文件，并选择分析配置：Surface QA、FEM QA 或 Additive Manufacturing。配置决定第 3、5 步使用的阈值。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "2. 表面完整性"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "报告顶点/面/边数量、是否水密、是否流形、边界边数、非流形边数、重复面、退化面、重复顶点、朝向一致性、Euler 示性数、亏格、表面积与封闭体积。勾选「检查自相交」后会额外做三角形两两求交（较慢）；若候选对数超出预算，会明确标注「搜索被截断，结果不完整」。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "3. 单元质量"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "按指标给出最小/最大/平均值，以及在当前配置阈值下的合格/警告/不合格计数，并列出最差的 25 个单元。加载了体网格时，四面体与六面体的体积、scaled Jacobian、二面角和反转单元一并计算。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "4. 可打印性"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "给定打印方向后，报告悬垂面数与面积、构建宽/深/高与占地面积、锐边数量、以及射线法测得的壁厚最小值与中位数。「运行朝向扫描」会在球面上均匀取若干方向，按悬垂面积（其次按高度）排名，结果是**确定性**的。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "5. 复查与修复"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "列出在当前配置下不合格的单元及其触发原因。本插件只负责**诊断**：补洞、重网格化、抽稀等修复操作请使用 PyMeshLab 插件，不在此重复实现。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "6. 发布与导出"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "把结果写回原网格的标量槽、发布只含不合格单元的网格副本，或导出 CSV、VTP、自包含 HTML 报告。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "使用步骤",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "在第 1 步选择网格并选定分析配置。",
            "在第 2 步点击「运行表面检查」。若网格不水密或存在非流形边，先记下来——后续的体积与可打印性判断会受影响。",
            "在第 3 步点击「运行单元质量」，查看不合格计数与最差单元列表。",
            "在第 4 步设置打印方向与悬垂角上限，点击「运行可打印性」；如需寻找更好的朝向，再点「运行朝向扫描」。",
            "在第 5 步核对不合格单元清单。",
            "在第 6 步写回标量、发布问题单元副本或导出报告。"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "任何时候都可以回到前面的步骤修改参数；插件会自动清空受影响的下游结果并提示需要重新运行。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "参数说明",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "参数",
              "默认值",
              "范围",
              "说明"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "分析配置",
                "Surface QA",
                "Surface QA / FEM QA / Additive Manufacturing",
                "决定第 3、5 步的合格/警告/不合格阈值"
              ],
              [
                "检查自相交",
                "关闭",
                "开 / 关",
                "三角形两两求交，较慢；超出候选预算时会标注结果不完整"
              ],
              [
                "打印方向",
                "0, 0, 1",
                "各分量 −1…1",
                "构建方向；悬垂与构建尺寸都相对它计算"
              ],
              [
                "悬垂角上限",
                "45",
                "0…89 度",
                "墙面相对竖直方向允许的最大倾角，超过即判为需要支撑"
              ],
              [
                "锐边角度",
                "80",
                "0…180 度",
                "相邻面法向夹角超过该值即计为锐边"
              ],
              [
                "壁厚采样数",
                "4000",
                "0…200000",
                "射线法采样的面数；设为 0 则跳过壁厚计算"
              ],
              [
                "朝向扫描方向数",
                "64",
                "4…512",
                "球面上均匀取向的数量，越多越细但越慢"
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "输出结果",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**网格标量槽**：`MQ Aspect Ratio`、`MQ Min Angle`、`MQ Scaled Jacobian`、`MQ Skewness`、`MQ Face Slope`（度）、`MQ Overhang`。逐面指标按面积加权散布到顶点。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**问题单元网格副本**：一个新发布的网格，只包含在当前配置下不合格的面（顶点已压缩重编号）。原网格不被修改。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**CSV**：逐面全部指标；未运行单元质量时导出表面完整性汇总。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**VTP**：带逐单元标量的表面文件，可在 ParaView 中打开。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**HTML**：自包含报告，只包含**实际运行过**的步骤。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "常见问题与故障排除",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**列表里没有我的网格。** 列表只显示**已发布**的对象。请先发布该网格，再点第 1 步的「刷新」。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**壁厚显示「未计算」。** 采样数被设为 0，或该环境缺少 trimesh。顶部 Environment 一行会写明是哪一种。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**封闭体积显示「—」。** 只有水密网格的封闭体积才有意义；先在第 2 步确认水密性。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**自相交结果标注「搜索被截断」。** 候选三角形对数超过预算，结果不完整；请先减面或分块检查，不要把它当作「没有自相交」。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**体网格文件加载后没有单元质量结果。** 目前从文件读取的体网格支持四面体与六面体；其他单元类型会被跳过。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "注意事项与已知限制",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "本插件只做**诊断**，不做修复。补洞、重网格化、抽稀请用 PyMeshLab 插件。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "`distortion` 指标由 VTK 提供；本插件刻意不自行实现该指标（Verdict 定义需要完整 Jacobian，自行近似会产生同名但不可比的数值）。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "六面体体积由五个四面体求和得到，对严重扭曲的单元只是**估计值**。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "壁厚为射线法测量，是沿面法向反方向到对面的距离；它与 VertexMeasurements 的局部厚度定义不同，两者不可直接互换。"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "从 Dragonfly 对象直接读取体网格连通性在部分版本上不可用；此时请改用 `.vtu` 文件输入，插件会明确提示。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "参考资料",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "VTK `vtkMeshQuality`：https://vtk.org/doc/nightly/html/classvtkMeshQuality.html"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Verdict 几何质量库（VTK 中的参考实现）"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Blender 3D-Print Toolbox（仅作为功能需求参考，未使用其源码）：https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/3.6/addons/mesh/3d_print_toolbox.html"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "This plugin checks a published surface mesh the way a **solver** or a **3D printer** will, optionally together with a volumetric grid loaded from a `.vtu` / `.vtk` file. It never modifies your input: every result is either a new scalar slot on the mesh or a newly published object."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The panel is six numbered steps. A step stays disabled until its inputs exist, and changing anything upstream invalidates the results below it, so an exported number always matches the settings on screen."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "All element-quality metrics follow the **Verdict** definitions (VTK's `vtkMeshQuality` is the reference implementation) and are cross-checked value-by-value by automated tests, so a number here is directly comparable with any other Verdict-based tool."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the first tab runs the workflow unattended - surface, mesh quality, printability - each step with whatever its own tab shows when you press it. Three steps are tick boxes and all three are OFF by default: the orientation sweep, because it runs up to 512 full overhang analyses, and the two publishing steps, because they write to the session. Every tab stays open so the thresholds and the print settings can be read and changed BEFORE the run; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses when you press ITS button and says which step is missing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Use cases",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "FEM pre-processing: confirm there are no **inverted cells**, extreme aspect ratios or tiny minimum angles."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Additive manufacturing: evaluate **overhang area** and **minimum wall thickness** for a build direction, and let the plugin sweep for a better one."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "After segmenting industrial CT: verify the reconstructed mesh is **watertight** and free of **self-intersections** before simulation or printing."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Locate what to repair: publish a mesh copy containing only the failing elements and see the problem in the 3D view."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Installation & enabling",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "Install the Prototype Apps package (or tick this plugin in the App Store).",
            "The plugin is **disabled by default** — enable it in the App Store or the Menu Item Manager.",
            "**Restart Dragonfly completely** (plugins are discovered at startup only).",
            "Open it from Prototype Apps ▸ Mesh Element Quality & Printability… (group: Simulation & Meshing)."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Runtime environment & first-run setup",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Nothing to install or configure.** The plugin runs entirely inside Dragonfly's own Python using the VTK 9.4.2 and trimesh it already ships. No internet, no download, no GPU, no virtual environment."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The **Environment** line at the top of the panel reports three capabilities live: the VTK version, whether scalar write-back is available, and whether wall thickness can be computed (it needs trimesh). Anything unavailable disables the matching feature and says why, rather than returning a wrong answer."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Interface",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "A fixed header shows the environment, the current input, the current task, a progress bar and **Cancel**. Long analyses run on a worker thread so the UI stays responsive, and a cancelled or failed run publishes nothing."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "1. Setup & Source"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Pick a **published** mesh (the list shows published objects only), optionally point at a `.vtu` / `.vtk` volumetric grid, and choose an analysis profile: Surface QA, FEM QA or Additive Manufacturing. The profile supplies the thresholds used in steps 3 and 5."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "2. Surface Integrity"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Reports vertex/face/edge counts, watertightness, manifoldness, boundary and non-manifold edges, duplicate and degenerate faces, duplicate vertices, orientation consistency, Euler characteristic, genus, surface area and enclosed volume. Ticking self-intersection adds a pairwise triangle test (slow); if the candidate budget is exhausted the result is explicitly marked as truncated and incomplete."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "3. Element Quality"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Min/max/mean per metric plus OK / warn / fail counts under the active profile, and the 25 worst elements. When a volumetric grid is loaded, tet and hex volume, scaled Jacobian, dihedral angles and inverted-cell detection are computed too."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "4. Printability"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "For the chosen build direction: overhang face count and area, build width/depth/height and footprint, sharp-edge count, and ray-cast wall thickness (minimum and median). The orientation sweep samples directions uniformly on the sphere and ranks them by overhang area then height — the ranking is **deterministic**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "5. Review & Repair"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Lists the elements that fail the active profile and why. This plugin **diagnoses only**: hole filling, remeshing and decimation live in the PyMeshLab plugin and are not duplicated here."
        },
        {
          "kind": "h3",
          "text": "6. Publish & Export"
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Write the results back as scalar slots, publish a mesh copy containing only the failing elements, or export CSV, VTP and a self-contained HTML report."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "In step 1 select the mesh and the analysis profile.",
            "In step 2 click Run surface checks. If the mesh is not watertight or has non-manifold edges, note it — volume and printability answers depend on it.",
            "In step 3 click Run element quality and read the fail counts and the worst-element list.",
            "In step 4 set the build direction and overhang limit and click Run printability; click Run orientation sweep to look for a better direction.",
            "In step 5 review the failing elements.",
            "In step 6 write the scalars back, publish the failed-element copy, or export a report."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "You can go back to an earlier step at any time; the plugin clears the results that depended on what you changed and tells you to re-run."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Parameters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Parameter",
              "Default",
              "Range",
              "Meaning"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Analysis profile",
                "Surface QA",
                "Surface QA / FEM QA / Additive Manufacturing",
                "Supplies the OK / warn / fail thresholds used in steps 3 and 5"
              ],
              [
                "Check self-intersections",
                "off",
                "on / off",
                "Pairwise triangle intersection test; slow, and marked incomplete if the candidate budget is exhausted"
              ],
              [
                "Build direction",
                "0, 0, 1",
                "each component −1…1",
                "Build-up direction; overhangs and build dimensions are measured relative to it"
              ],
              [
                "Overhang limit",
                "45",
                "0…89 deg",
                "How far a wall may lean from vertical before it needs support"
              ],
              [
                "Sharp edge angle",
                "80",
                "0…180 deg",
                "An edge counts as sharp when the angle between its two face normals exceeds this"
              ],
              [
                "Wall thickness samples",
                "4000",
                "0…200000",
                "Number of faces sampled by the ray cast; 0 skips thickness entirely"
              ],
              [
                "Sweep directions",
                "64",
                "4…512",
                "Directions sampled uniformly on the sphere; more is finer but slower"
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Output",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Mesh scalar slots**: `MQ Aspect Ratio`, `MQ Min Angle`, `MQ Scaled Jacobian`, `MQ Skewness`, `MQ Face Slope` (degrees) and `MQ Overhang`. Per-face metrics are scattered to vertices with area weighting."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Failed-element mesh copy**: a newly published mesh containing only the faces that fail the active profile, with vertices compacted. The original mesh is untouched."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**CSV**: every metric per face; if element quality has not been run, the surface-integrity summary is exported instead."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**VTP**: the surface with per-cell scalars, ready to open in ParaView."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**HTML**: a self-contained report containing only the steps that actually ran."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "FAQ & troubleshooting",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**My mesh is not in the list.** The list shows **published** objects only. Publish the mesh, then press Refresh in step 1."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Wall thickness says not computed.** Either the sample count is 0 or trimesh is missing in this environment; the Environment line at the top says which."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Enclosed volume shows a dash.** Enclosed volume is only meaningful for a watertight mesh — check step 2 first."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Self-intersection says the search was truncated.** The candidate budget was exhausted, so the result is incomplete; decimate or check in blocks, and do not read it as 'no self-intersections'."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**A loaded volumetric grid produced no element quality.** Grids read from file currently support tetrahedra and hexahedra; other cell types are skipped."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Notes & known limitations",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "This plugin **diagnoses only** — hole filling, remeshing and decimation belong to the PyMeshLab plugin."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "The `distortion` metric comes from VTK. It is deliberately not reimplemented here: the Verdict definition needs the full Jacobian, and a look-alike approximation under the same name would not be comparable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Hex volume is the sum of five tetrahedra, which is an **estimate** for badly warped cells."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Wall thickness is a ray cast along the inward face normal to the opposite wall. That is a different definition from VertexMeasurements' local thickness, and the two are not interchangeable."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Reading volumetric cell connectivity straight from a Dragonfly object is not available on every build; the plugin says so and asks you to use the `.vtu` file input instead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "References",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "VTK `vtkMeshQuality`: https://vtk.org/doc/nightly/html/classvtkMeshQuality.html"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "The Verdict geometric quality library (the reference implementation inside VTK)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Blender 3D-Print Toolbox (used only as a reference for which checks matter; no source was copied): https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/3.6/addons/mesh/3d_print_toolbox.html"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Create a Report from Mesh",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：选择一个已发布的 Mesh，把它的**全部 measurements** 整理成一份报告（xlsx 或 pptx）。**Mesh 的 measurements 分两大类，报告中严格分开呈现，因为二者不可比**：**顶点类（vertex-based）**——每个网格顶点一个值，是分布在表面上的连续场（如局部厚度、曲率），统计量描述的是表面采样点云，N = 顶点数；**标签类（label-based）**——每个标签（分割出的子对象）一个值，是每个部件一个数（如每颗颗粒的体积、表面积），统计量描述的是一个对象总体，N = 标签数，且每个值都归属一个具名标签。报告包含：总览（按类分表/分页，列出每个 measurement 的均值/中位数/最小/最大/标准差/单位/N）、每个 measurement 的直方图、以及仅显示该 Mesh 并按该 measurement 着色的 3D 截图；标签类还额外列出每个标签的具体数值。**新增“为每个 measurement 添加动画 GIF”选项**：勾选后对每个 measurement 从 8 个不同角度（角度数与帧间隔可调）拍摄 3D 渲染截图，合成为一个循环播放的动画 GIF 放进报告——pptx 中直接嵌入 GIF（放映时会自动旋转播放），xlsx 中放入首帧静态图并标注 GIF 文件名。若该 Mesh 还带有面类（face-based）标量槽，报告会注明其数量（不纳入统计）。\n\n**分享到网页(新增)**：报告还可以生成为**单个 HTML 文件**并上传到免费静态托管（GitHub Pages / Netlify / Gitee Pages，用你自己的账号），上传后面板上直接显示可访问的 URL，可一键复制到剪贴板，并显示二维码供扫码分享；随时可以“撤下”把已发布的文件删除。所有图片与旋转 GIF 都内嵌在这一个文件里，因此手机打开即可，不依赖任何外部资源。**可见性三档**：公开（任何人可见，可能被搜索引擎收录）／不公开（只有拿到链接的人可见：随机不可猜路径 + noindex）／密码保护（正文用 AES-256-GCM 加密，浏览器端输入口令解密；托管方只持有密文）。**口令永不保存**，请与链接分开发送。\n\n**分享报告标签页（新增）**：第二条、与上面相反的分享方式 —— 用 Cloudflare 快速隧道把同一个单文件报告直接从本机发布出去，无需账号、不上传，而且窗口一关地址就永久失效。它没有密码，因此适合让外网的人看几分钟，而不适合正式交付结果。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：把颗粒/孔隙/纤维分割后的 Mesh 测量结果一次性交付成可汇报的文档；向客户或同事展示表面场（厚度/曲率）与逐颗粒统计的差异；用旋转 GIF 直观呈现三维形貌与测量分布，避免单一视角造成的误读；批量归档测量结果。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需虚拟环境/GPU/管理员权限，纯进程内运行。需要会话中至少有一个已发布的 Mesh，且其上已计算过顶点类或标签类 measurement（可用 Compute Vertex Measurements / Compute Overall Measurements 等工具生成）。3D 截图与 GIF 需要在真实 Dragonfly 界面中运行（离屏无 3D 视图时会跳过截图，统计与直方图仍然生成）。xlsx 与直方图使用 Dragonfly 自带的 openpyxl/matplotlib，GIF 使用其自带 Pillow；pptx 首次使用会自动下载一次 python-pptx。 分享功能需要联网和一个你自己的托管账号：建议使用**细粒度 PAT，且只授权一个专用仓库**的 Contents 与 Pages 写权限，不要使用 classic 的 repo 全权令牌（令牌以明文保存在本机设置文件中）。GitHub Pages 免费版需要仓库为公开，且每次发布后构建需要 10–60 秒；Gitee 免费版发布后需要到仓库的 Pages 页面手动点一次“更新”。二维码与加密使用 Dragonfly 自带的 qrcode 与 cryptography，无需额外安装。「分享报告」标签页需要本机能访问外网，并需要 Cloudflare 的 cloudflared.exe；它没有被打包在内，会在你确认后下载一次（约 52 MB）并按用户保存。快速隧道是 Cloudflare 自己的测试设施 —— 有速率限制且不承诺可用性 —— 因此标签页会明确告知该地址是否已在本机确认可用。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: pick a published Mesh and turn ALL of its measurements into a report (xlsx or pptx). **Mesh measurements come in two families and the report keeps them strictly apart, because they are not comparable**: **VERTEX-BASED** — one value per mesh vertex, i.e. a continuous field sampled over the surface (e.g. local thickness or curvature); statistics describe that cloud of surface samples and N equals the vertex count. **LABEL-BASED** — one value per label, i.e. per segmented sub-object (e.g. a volume or an area per particle); statistics describe a population of objects, N equals the label count, and every value belongs to a named label. The report contains an overview (separate table/slide per family, listing mean/median/min/max/std/unit/N per measurement), a histogram per measurement, and a 3D screenshot showing only that Mesh coloured by the measurement; label-based sheets additionally list every label's value. **New option 'Add animated GIF for each measurement'**: when ticked, each measurement is captured from 8 different angles (angle count and frame delay adjustable) of the 3D rendering and the frames are combined into one looping animated GIF — embedded directly in pptx (PowerPoint animates it in slideshow mode) and represented in xlsx by its first frame plus the GIF filename. If the Mesh also carries face-based scalar slots, the report states how many (they are not analysed).\n\n**Share on the web (new)**: the report can also be built as ONE self-contained HTML file and uploaded to free static hosting (GitHub Pages / Netlify / Gitee Pages, using your own account). The panel then shows the working URL, copies it to the clipboard on one click, and displays a QR code for sharing; \"Take it down\" deletes the published file again. Every image and rotation GIF is embedded in that single file, so it opens on a phone with no external resources. **Three visibility levels**: public (anyone, may be indexed by search engines) / unlisted (only people with the link - an unguessable random path plus noindex) / password protected (the body is AES-256-GCM encrypted and decrypted in the viewer's browser, so the host holds ciphertext only). **The password is never saved** - send it separately from the link.\n\n**Share Report tab (new)**: a SECOND, opposite way to share - a Cloudflare quick tunnel that publishes the same one-file report straight from this machine, with no account and no upload, and whose address stops working permanently the moment the window is closed. It has no password, so it is for letting somebody outside take a look for a few minutes, not for delivering results.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: deliver the measurement results of a segmented particle/pore/fibre Mesh as a ready-to-share document; show colleagues or customers the difference between a surface field (thickness/curvature) and per-object statistics; use the rotating GIF to convey 3D morphology and the spatial distribution of a measurement without the bias of a single viewpoint; archive measurement results in batches.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no venv/GPU/admin — pure in-process. Needs at least one published Mesh carrying vertex-based or label-based measurements (compute them first with e.g. Compute Vertex Measurements / Compute Overall Measurements). 3D screenshots and GIFs need a live Dragonfly GUI (without a 3D view the screenshots are skipped and statistics/histograms are still produced). xlsx and histograms use Dragonfly's own openpyxl/matplotlib and GIFs its Pillow; pptx downloads python-pptx once on first use. Sharing needs internet access and your own hosting account: use a **fine-grained PAT scoped to ONE dedicated repository** with Contents and Pages write access - never a classic all-repository token (the token is stored in plain text in the local settings file). Free GitHub Pages requires a public repository and takes 10-60 s to build after each publish; on Gitee's free tier you must click 更新 once on the repository's Pages page. QR codes and encryption use the qrcode and cryptography packages Dragonfly already ships - nothing extra to install. The Share Report tab needs outbound internet access and Cloudflare's cloudflared.exe, which is not bundled: it is downloaded once (about 52 MB) with your confirmation and kept per user. A quick tunnel is Cloudflare's own test facility - rate-limited and with no availability promise - so the tab reports whether the address was actually confirmed working from this machine."
  }
}

