  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Segmentation QA (3D)** answers one concrete question: *how good is this segmentation?* It treats one **published MultiROI or ROI** as the **ground truth** and another as the **segmentation to evaluate**, then reports the standard agreement metrics - computed over the **whole 3D volume**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "This reimplements the metric set of the ImageJ plugin **MiC** (MIT, https://github.com/MultimodalImagingCenter/MiC). MiC’s README says it works only in 2D, but **that line is stale relative to its own code** — MiC ships a registered “Mask instant Comparator 3D” entry, so **3D is not the differentiator**. What this plugin actually offers is running inside Dragonfly on **published MultiROI/ROI** objects, with results wired into Dragonfly’s own tables, overlays and reports, plus **boundary distances in world units** (ASSD / Hausdorff), which MiC does not compute. The per-slice mode is kept so results can be compared with the ImageJ original."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The two inputs must come from the **same image grid** (identical shape). A mismatch is reported as an explicit error naming both shapes - never as silently wrong numbers."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Every tab can be opened and edited at any time, and no tab is ever locked shut. The Export button in particular is no longer greyed out before a comparison exists: it stays live and, when pressed, says that there is nothing to export yet and which step produces it - a disabled button cannot tell you why it is disabled. There is deliberately no 'Execute All Steps' button here, because there is only one compute step: the Compare button already does read, measure and optionally publish in a single press, the results tab is a passive view, and the only other action writes files to a folder you must choose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two levels of metric, and why accuracy is not reported",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Voxel level**: TP (both call it foreground), FP (only the evaluated mask does - over-segmentation), FN (only the ground truth does - missed), then precision = TP/(TP+FP), recall = TP/(TP+FN), Jaccard (IoU) = TP/(TP+FP+FN) and F1 = 2TP/(2TP+FP+FN), which is the same number as the Dice coefficient."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Accuracy and specificity are deliberately NOT reported.** Both need TN, the voxels both sides call background - and in a volume that is often over 99% of the data, so any TN-based score reads above 0.99 no matter how bad the segmentation is. Reporting it would only mislead."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Object level**: every ground-truth object is matched **one-to-one** with a predicted object by IoU, then counted across a sweep of IoU thresholds: a matched pair with IoU >= threshold is a TP, an unmatched prediction is an FP, an unmatched ground-truth object is an FN. The default sweep is 0.50 to 0.95 in steps of 0.05 (the COCO and StarDist/Cellpose convention). From those counts: **AP = TP/(TP+FP+FN)**, its mean over the sweep **mAP**, and **panoptic quality PQ** = (sum of matched IoU) / (TP + FP/2 + FN/2)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**mAP is only meaningful when BOTH inputs are labelled MultiROIs.** With a binary ROI the whole foreground is one object, so only the voxel-level metrics apply."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Matching: greedy or optimal",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Matching is GREEDY by descending IoU by default (what the ImageJ MiC original does), and **at IoU thresholds >= 0.5 greedy is provably optimal** - one prediction cannot exceed 0.5 IoU with two ground-truth objects at once. The results panel always states which rule produced the numbers."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "\"Maximise TOTAL IoU (Hungarian)\" is **off by default and not recommended**: it optimises the SUM of IoU, while these metrics count PAIRS ABOVE THE THRESHOLD - a different objective. Measured case: with IoUs 0.5556 / 0.2857 / 0.2857 it discards the 0.5556 pair (0.2857+0.2857 is a larger sum) and reports TP/FP/FN = 0/2/2 and mAP 0.0000 at IoU 0.50, where the correct answer is non-zero."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Boundary distances (optional)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "When ticked, the plugin also reports **ASSD** (average symmetric surface distance), **95% Hausdorff** and maximum Hausdorff, **scaled by the voxel spacing** so the numbers are world units even for anisotropic voxels."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Why it is worth having: two masks can share a Dice of 0.9 and still be a whole voxel off everywhere. Volume-overlap metrics cannot see that; a boundary distance shows it immediately. Upstream MiC has no equivalent. Needs scipy; if either mask is empty the result is reported as \"not computed\" rather than as 0."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use it",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "1. **Publish** both segmentations into the session - the plugin lists published objects only."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "2. Open **Prototype Apps > Segmentation QA: Compare Masks in 3D...** and pick the ground truth and the prediction on tab 1. Press Refresh if the lists are empty."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "3. Adjust the IoU sweep if needed, tick per-slice comparison / boundary distances / publish overlay, then press **Compare now**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "4. Tab 2 shows a one-line headline (voxel Dice, Jaccard, object counts, mAP, matching method), the full metric table, and the per-threshold object table."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "5. Tab 3 exports Excel/CSV/JSON and the plots to a folder of your choice."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The TP/FP/FN overlay",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "With \"Publish a TP/FP/FN overlay MultiROI when done\" ticked, a new MultiROI is created and published with three labels: **TP (agree) green**, **FP (extra) red**, **FN (missed) blue**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "This is the most useful part of the plugin: the numbers say how much is wrong, the overlay says where. Red rims around every object means the segmentation is systematically too fat; blue where the small objects are means they were missed; no blue boundary between two touching objects means the model merged them."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The overlay inherits the source spacing and origin, so it lines up exactly in the 2D/3D views. If the two segmentations agree everywhere (no FP or FN voxel at all) the plugin says so instead of publishing an empty object."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Requirements and limits",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "No GPU, no internet, no admin rights and nothing to install: everything runs inside Dragonfly on the bundled numpy. Optimal matching and boundary distances need scipy, Excel export needs openpyxl, plots need matplotlib - all shipped with Dragonfly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Limits: the two inputs must have the same shape; for a time series compare one time point at a time (the plugin reads the current one); object-level metrics need labels, so a binary ROI supports voxel-level evaluation only."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "MONAI Label Segmentation",
  "cn": {
    "func": "该插件在 Dragonfly 内提供一个原生可停靠面板,连接(本机或远程的)MONAI Label 服务器做交互式 AI 分割。连接后自动从 /info 读取模型/策略/标签填充下拉框。选择一个 Channel 并【加载】(在进程内读为 numpy 体数据),在内嵌切片查看器里滚动层面:【左键=前景点、右键=背景点】(整数体素坐标 [i,j,k])。点【Run】把体数据导出为 NIfTI(内置纯 numpy 编解码,无需 SimpleITK)、连同点位发给 /infer/{model}——DeepEdit/DeepGrow 用几个点就能补全整卷分割;不点任何点则为纯自动分割。结果 mask 叠加显示,确认后【一键导入为 MultiROI】(在源 Channel 网格上,优先 CellposeHelper,回退 Channel→getAsMultiROI)。第二阶段【主动学习】:点【Next best volume】,服务器按不确定性(如 epistemic)给未标注卷排序,告诉你下一个最该标哪一卷。REST 协议来自共用的 monailabel_client 模块。",
    "scenarios": "适用于医学/临床前/生命科学的 CT/MRI 体数据分割:用少量点击快速得到整卷器官/病灶分割(远快于逐层手标),再导入 Dragonfly 做后续分析或作为训练标注;面对一大批扫描时,用主动学习决定最先标注哪一卷以最大化每份标注的收益。",
    "requirements": "需要一个可访问的 MONAI Label 服务器(在 Prototype Apps > Server Management 里启动【MONAI Label Server】——它会自动建 venv、装 torch 与 monailabel、下载 radiology 应用;或把面板 URL 指向运行中的/远程服务器,默认 127.0.0.1:8384)。插件本身无 venv,运行于 Dragonfly 自带 Python(自带 numpy;NIfTI 读写为内置纯 numpy 编解码)。界面协议来自 monailabel_client.py,请同时安装 Prototype Labs 嵌入式包。主动学习/提交修正需要把扫描放入服务器的 studies 数据仓。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "A native dockable panel, inside Dragonfly, for interactive AI segmentation against a (local or remote) MONAI Label server. On Connect it reads /info to fill the model / strategy / label dropdowns. Pick a Channel and Load it (read to numpy in-process); scroll slices in the embedded viewer and LEFT-click = foreground, RIGHT-click = background points (integer voxel [i,j,k]). 'Run' exports the volume to NIfTI (a built-in pure-numpy codec — no SimpleITK), POSTs it with the click params to /infer/{model} — DeepEdit/DeepGrow complete the whole-volume mask from a few clicks; no clicks = pure auto-segmentation. The result overlays on the viewer, and 'Import as MultiROI' publishes it on the source Channel's grid (CellposeHelper first, Channel->getAsMultiROI fallback). Phase 2 = active learning: 'Next best volume' asks the server to rank unlabeled studies by uncertainty (e.g. epistemic) and tells you which to annotate next. The REST protocol is the shared monailabel_client module.",
    "scenarios": "For medical / preclinical / life-science CT & MRI segmentation: get a whole-volume organ/lesion mask from a few clicks (far faster than slice-by-slice manual labeling) and import it into Dragonfly for analysis or as training labels; with a large cohort, use active learning to decide which volume to annotate first so each label maximizes model improvement.",
    "requirements": "Needs a reachable MONAI Label server (start one in Prototype Apps > Server Management: 'MONAI Label Server' — it auto-creates a venv, installs torch + monailabel, downloads the radiology app; or point the panel URL at a running/remote server, default 127.0.0.1:8384). The plugin itself has no venv; it runs in Dragonfly's own Python (bundled numpy; NIfTI I/O is a built-in pure-numpy codec). The UI protocol comes from monailabel_client.py — also install the Prototype Labs embedded package. Active learning / submitting corrections needs your scans in the server's studies datastore."
  }
}

{
  "title": "MorphoLibJ Remade by Python",
  "cn": {
    "func": "把 MorphoLibJ 的核心分割流程用 Python 重新实现，直接在 Dragonfly ROI 上运行，不再依赖 ImageJ、Fiji 或 Java。当前版本覆盖连通域标记、距离变换分水岭、marker generation、watershed，以及 opening/closing/fill holes 后的连通域拆分；结果作为 Dragonfly MultiROI 导入。",
    "scenarios": "适用于希望复用 MorphoLibJ 风格的二值 ROI 拆分、接触对象分离、孔隙/颗粒/细胞区域分割，但不希望安装或调用 Fiji/ImageJ 的用户。",
    "requirements": "首次使用需要在插件 Setup tab 中创建独立 venv 并安装 numpy、scipy、scikit-image；安装时需要联网。运行时不需要 GPU、Fiji、ImageJ 或 Java。在 Dragonfly 2027.1（Python 3.14）上不能用 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 创建该环境：请安装 python.org 的 Python（3.12、3.13 或 3.14）并填入面板的 Base Python；Dragonfly 2025.1 无需另装 Python。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Reimplements core MorphoLibJ-style segmentation directly in Python for Dragonfly ROIs, without ImageJ, Fiji, or Java. The current version covers connected-components labeling, distance-transform watershed, marker generation, watershed, and opening/closing/fill-holes followed by connected components; the output is imported as a Dragonfly MultiROI.",
    "scenarios": "For users who want MorphoLibJ-style binary ROI splitting, touching-object separation, and pore/grain/cell-region segmentation without installing or calling Fiji/ImageJ.",
    "requirements": "First use builds an isolated plugin venv and installs numpy, scipy, and scikit-image from PyPI; internet is needed for setup. Normal processing requires no GPU, Fiji, ImageJ, or Java. On Dragonfly 2027.1 (Python 3.14) the bundled Python cannot build this environment: install a python.org Python (3.12, 3.13 or 3.14) and enter it in the panel's Base Python field; Dragonfly 2025.1 needs no separate Python."
  }
}

{
  "title": "MorphoLibJ via Fiji",
  "cn": {
    "func": "在 Dragonfly 中选择一个 ROI，把它导出为 Fiji 可读取的二值 TIFF，在本机 Fiji 中调用 MorphoLibJ 执行连通域标记、距离变换分水岭或形态学预处理，再把 Fiji 输出的标签图导入回 Dragonfly 并转换为 MultiROI。面板会自动查找 Fiji，也可以手动指定 Fiji/ImageJ 启动器。",
    "scenarios": "适用于已经有 Dragonfly ROI、希望复用 Fiji MorphoLibJ 分割与形态学算法来生成对象级 MultiROI 的用户，例如孔隙/颗粒/细胞区域的连通域拆分、分水岭分割和形态学清理。",
    "requirements": "需要本机已安装 Fiji/ImageJ。MorphoLibJ 通过 Fiji 的 IJPB-plugins 更新站点提供；如果面板检测不到 MorphoLibJ，会弹窗询问是否先安装该 Fiji 插件。安装/更新 MorphoLibJ 时需要联网；正常运行不需要 Python 虚拟环境或 GPU。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Select a Dragonfly ROI, export it as a Fiji-readable binary TIFF, run MorphoLibJ in the user's local Fiji for connected-components labeling, distance-transform watershed, or morphology-assisted labeling, then import the Fiji label image back into Dragonfly as a MultiROI. The panel can auto-detect Fiji or use a user-selected Fiji/ImageJ launcher.",
    "scenarios": "For users who already have a Dragonfly ROI and want to reuse Fiji MorphoLibJ segmentation and morphology tools to produce object-level MultiROIs, such as separating pores, grains, cells, or cleaned connected components.",
    "requirements": "Requires a local Fiji/ImageJ installation. MorphoLibJ is provided by Fiji's IJPB-plugins update site; if the panel cannot detect MorphoLibJ, it prompts the user to install that Fiji plugin first. Internet is needed for installation/update only; normal processing needs no Python virtual environment or GPU."
  }
}

{
  "title": "Digital Image Correlation 2D (muDIC)",
  "cn": {
    "func": "对二维图像序列进行全场数字图像相关（DIC）分析。选择一个 Channel（其 Z 或 T 轴为一组二维帧图像），设置参考帧序号、网格单元尺寸、ROI 范围与应变度量后点击计算；插件基于 muDIC 构建 Q4 网格并运行 DICAnalysis，输出每一帧相对参考帧的位移场（u、v）与应变场（exx、eyy、exy）标量 Channel，以及汇总统计表，可用色图显示位移与应变分布。区别于三维体积相关的 SPAM-DVC 插件。",
    "scenarios": "适用于材料力学与实验力学中的二维全场变形测量——拉伸/压缩试验的应变分布、裂纹尖端场、复合材料与薄板变形、原位加载 CT/显微序列的表面变形分析等。",
    "requirements": "首次使用点击 Setup Environment（默认使用 Dragonfly 自带 Python 构建本地计算环境，联网安装 muDIC/numpy/scipy/matplotlib，仅需一次）。无需 GPU。在 Dragonfly 2027.1（Python 3.14）上不能用 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 创建该环境：请安装 python.org 的 Python（3.12、3.13 或 3.14）并填入面板的 Base Python；Dragonfly 2025.1 无需另装 Python。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Full-field 2D Digital Image Correlation (DIC) of an image sequence. Pick a Channel whose Z (or T) axis is a stack of 2D frames, set the reference frame index, mesh element size, ROI extent, and strain measure, then Compute; the plugin builds a Q4 mesh and runs muDIC's DICAnalysis, producing per-frame displacement (u, v) and strain (exx, eyy, exy) field Channels plus a summary table you can display with a colormap. Distinct from the 3D SPAM-DVC (volume correlation) plugin.",
    "scenarios": "2D full-field deformation measurement in materials and experimental mechanics - strain fields in tensile/compression tests, crack-tip fields, composites and sheet-metal deformation, and surface deformation from in-situ loading CT/microscopy image sequences.",
    "requirements": "First use: click Setup Environment (builds a local compute environment from Dragonfly's own Python by default and installs muDIC/numpy/scipy/matplotlib over the internet, one time). No GPU required. On Dragonfly 2027.1 (Python 3.14) the bundled Python cannot build this environment: install a python.org Python (3.12, 3.13 or 3.14) and enter it in the panel's Base Python field; Dragonfly 2025.1 needs no separate Python."
  }
}

{
 "title": "Multi-ROI Export",
 "cn": {
  "func": "功能：在窗口顶部**只选一次 Multi-ROI**（及其时间步），再用三个选项卡以三种方式把它导出——同一时间只运行其中一个。**① 单个 STL 文件**：每个标签先提取为**临时 ROI**（不发布），用 **Dragonfly 自带的 marching cubes**（ROI.getAsMarchingCubesMesh）生成网格，**每个标签写成一个 STL 文件**；可设采样 X/Y/Z、先填充内部空腔、拉普拉斯平滑，二进制或 ASCII，单位毫米（默认）/ 微米 / 米；“最终文件名”一列事先显示实际写入的名称，重名自动加 _1、_2，**绝不覆盖已有文件**。**② NIfTI (.nii)**：把勾选的标签写成**一个 NIfTI 标签图**（.nii 或 .nii.gz），文件头标明是标签图（intent = label，8/16/32 位整数，从不使用浮点），数值沿用 Dragonfly 的标签编号或**按 1..K 连续重新编号（用于机器学习，如 nnU-Net）**；位置、旋转与 Dragonfly 中一致，单位毫米，坐标系为 **RAS，与 ITK / SimpleITK 的写法相同**，因此与图像导出（Image Exporter）插件导出的同一数据的 NIfTI / NRRD / MetaImage 图像完全重合；同时写出 **ITK-SNAP 标签文件、3D Slicer 颜色表（CSV）和 JSON（含 nnU-Net labels 段）**。**③ 报告**（原插件“Create a Report from MultiROI / 从 MultiROI 生成报告”已并入此选项卡）：为该 Multi-ROI 已有的**全部测量**生成 **Excel / PowerPoint / Word / PDF** 报告——总览表（平均值、中位数、最小值、最大值、**总体标准差**、单位、N），每项测量一页，含**直方图**和按该测量着色的**三维截图**（默认开启）；截图后布局、可见性、着色、图例、相机和当前视图**全部恢复原状**；还可把报告**分享到网页**（GitHub Pages / Netlify / Gitee，二维码，可设密码）或生成 **Cloudflare 临时链接**。**不向会话添加任何对象。**",
  "scenarios": "典型场景：把分割得到的多相材料、颗粒、孔隙、骨骼/牙齿、器官或零件的每个类别分别导出为 STL，交给 CAD、3D 打印切片软件、有限元（FEA）或 CFD 前处理；把分割结果作为 NIfTI 标签图交给 nnU-Net、MONAI 等深度学习训练，或在 ITK-SNAP、3D Slicer 中打开并与原图像叠加检查；把一次孔隙/颗粒/晶粒分割的各项测量（体积、球形度、表面积、等效直径……）整理成可直接汇报的 Excel、PowerPoint、Word 或 PDF 报告，并按需在网页上分享给同事或客户。",
  "requirements": "运行要求：无需安装、无需虚拟环境、无需 GPU、无需管理员权限——进程内 PyQt6 加 Dragonfly 自带的 numpy、openpyxl、matplotlib，PowerPoint 所需的 python-pptx 1.0.2（MIT 许可）随插件提供，**无需下载**。Dragonfly 2025.1 与 2027.1 均可使用。需要会话中已发布一个 Multi-ROI；报告需要它已计算过测量，三维截图需要当前布局中有三维视图。只有“分享到网页”和“临时链接”需要联网，且只在你点击并确认后才会上传或下载（临时链接首次使用时经确认下载约 52 MB 的 cloudflared）。单层切片（2D）的 Multi-ROI 无法生成 STL 网格；NIfTI-1 每个轴最多 32767 个体素。"
 },
 "en": {
  "func": "What it does: **choose a Multi-ROI once** (and its time step) at the top of the window, then export it three ways, one tab each — only one runs at a time. **(1) Individual STL Files**: every label is extracted as a **temporary ROI** (never published), meshed with **Dragonfly's own marching cubes** (ROI.getAsMarchingCubesMesh) and written as **one STL file per label**; sampling X/Y/Z, inner-void filling and Laplacian smoothing, binary or ASCII, millimetres (default), micrometres or metres; a Final file name column shows every name before anything is written, a clash gets _1, _2, and **no existing file is ever overwritten**. **(2) NIfTI (.nii)**: the ticked labels as **ONE NIfTI label map** (.nii or .nii.gz) whose header marks it as a label map (intent = label, an 8-, 16- or 32-bit integer, never floating point), keeping Dragonfly's label numbers or **renumbering them 1..K for machine learning (e.g. nnU-Net)**; placed where Dragonfly places the Multi-ROI, rotation included, in millimetres and in **RAS exactly as ITK / SimpleITK write it**, so it overlays the Image Exporter's NIfTI, NRRD and MetaImage of the same data; with an **ITK-SNAP label file, a 3D Slicer colour table (CSV) and a JSON (with an nnU-Net labels block)** beside it. **(3) Report** (the former plugin 'Create a Report from MultiROI', retired into this tab): a report of **every measurement** the Multi-ROI carries as **Excel, PowerPoint, Word or PDF** — an overview (mean, median, min, max, **population standard deviation**, unit, N) and one page per measurement with a **histogram** and a **3-D screenshot** coloured by it (on by default); afterwards the layout, visibility, colouring, legends, camera and current view are **put back exactly**; the report can also be **shared on the web** (GitHub Pages / Netlify / Gitee, QR code, optional password) or through a **temporary Cloudflare link**. **Nothing is added to the session.**",
  "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: exporting each phase, particle, pore, bone or tooth, organ or part of a segmentation as its own STL for CAD, a 3D-printing slicer, FEA or CFD pre-processing; handing a segmentation to nnU-Net, MONAI or another training pipeline as a NIfTI label map, or opening it in ITK-SNAP or 3D Slicer over the original image; turning a pore / particle / grain segmentation's measurements (volume, sphericity, surface area, equivalent diameter, ...) into a deliverable Excel, PowerPoint, Word or PDF report, and sharing it on the web with colleagues or customers when needed.",
  "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no venv, no GPU, no admin — in-process PyQt6 plus the numpy, openpyxl and matplotlib Dragonfly already ships; python-pptx 1.0.2 (MIT) for PowerPoint ships with the plugin, so **nothing is downloaded**. Works in Dragonfly 2025.1 and 2027.1. A published Multi-ROI must be in the session; a report needs measurements computed on it, and its 3-D screenshots a layout with a 3-D view. Only 'Share the report on the web' and the temporary link need internet, and they upload or download nothing without a click and a confirmation (the temporary link downloads cloudflared, about 52 MB, once, after asking). A single-slice (2-D) Multi-ROI cannot be meshed as STL; NIfTI-1 holds at most 32767 voxels per axis."
 }
}

