  "en": {
    "func": "Trains a custom nnU-Net (v2) deep-learning segmentation model directly from your own Dragonfly data: you add one or more training cases, each consisting of an image Channel plus a MultiROI with the labeled classes, and the plugin trains a 3D model on your GPU. Once trained, you can apply the model to any Channel and the predicted segmentation is published back into the scene as a MultiROI, ready for measurement and visualization. nnU-Net automatically configures itself to your data, so no deep-learning expertise is required.\n\n**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the Setup tab runs the workflow unattended - set up the environment, add the case, train, infer - each step with whatever its own tab shows when you press it. Two steps are tick boxes and both are OFF by default: setting up the environment, because it builds a venv and downloads CUDA PyTorch and nnU-Net and never has to run twice, and training, because nnU-Net's default is a thousand epochs and hours of GPU time. The common unattended run is therefore 'predict with the model I already have'. Every tab stays open so the paths and parameters can be read and changed BEFORE the run; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses when you press ITS button and says which step is missing.",
    "scenarios": "Ideal whenever you need automated 3D segmentation tailored to your own samples: pores, cracks, fibers, or phases in materials-science and industrial CT scans; organs, cells, or tissue structures in life-science micro-CT and microscopy volumes; or defect detection in castings and additive-manufactured parts. Useful for anyone who repeatedly segments similar datasets and wants to label a few examples once, then segment the rest automatically.",
    "requirements": "First use: click Setup Environment (builds a Python environment with Dragonfly's own Python and downloads several GB); needs internet + an NVIDIA GPU (on Turing cards such as RTX 8000, use fp16, not bf16). On Dragonfly 2027.1 (Python 3.14) the bundled Python cannot build this environment: install a python.org Python (3.12; other versions not verified) and enter it in the panel's Base Python field; Dragonfly 2025.1 needs no separate Python."
