{
  "title": "Nominal-Actual Comparison (Hands-on Workshop)",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：一个工业 CT 计量的上手练习项目，讲清楚并动手跑通“名义-实测比对（CAD 对比 / 偏差分析）”的完整流水线。七个标签页 + 证书页：概念 → 加载 CAD（名义，STEP/STL）→ 加载 CT 三维图像（实测）→ 由实测生成表面网格（两条路线二选一：图像分割→ROI→网格，或亚体素 Surface Determination，并给出详细对照）→ 配准（最佳拟合 ICP）→ 偏差图（带符号最近距离，按公差着色）→ 结果与 Measurement Inspector（最大/均值/RMS、公差内比例、直方图）。核心动手环节在进程内用 numpy/skimage/trimesh 运行；按钮还能一键打开 Dragonfly 自带的 Surface Determination / Mesh Registration / Measurement Inspector 正式工具。\n\n第一个页签上的**一键执行全部步骤（按当前设置）**会无人值守地跑完整个比对流程：参考模型 → 实测体数据 → 提取曲面 → 配准 → 偏差 → 统计，每一步都使用你按下按钮那一刻各自页签上显示的设置。四个复选框的默认值遵循同一条原则：**凡是「制造数据」的步骤默认关闭，凡是「测量」的步骤默认开启**。生成合成参考模型（关闭）会替换掉你从文件载入的 CAD 模型；生成合成 CT 体数据（关闭）不但制造数据，还会把后面每一步所测量的那个 Channel 重新选走。提取曲面（开启）是测量本身的第一步——如果你想复用手工做好的曲面，取消勾选即可；偏差色图（开启）是本实践课的成果，统计步骤要从它读数。所有页签始终可以打开和修改参数，以便在运行**之前**逐页检查；某一步所需的输入尚不存在时，会在**它自己的按钮**上给出提示，说明缺的是哪一步，而不是把整个页签锁住不让进入。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：学习 CAD 对比 / 名义-实测偏差分析（首件检验、尺寸与形位检测、模具收缩/翘曲、增材制造质检、变形/磨损分析）；理解“图像分割”与“表面测定”两种从 CT 提取表面的方法差别；用自己的 CAD（STEP/STL）与 CT 数据走一遍偏差比对流程。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需安装、无需联网、无需 GPU、无需虚拟环境——用 Dragonfly 自带的 numpy/skimage/trimesh 在进程内运行。加载 STEP 文件需要 Dragonfly 2027.1 及以上（STL/OBJ/PLY 各版本均可）。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: a hands-on industrial-CT metrology project that teaches and runs the full Nominal-Actual comparison (CAD comparison / deviation analysis) pipeline. Seven tabs + a Certificate tab: Concepts → Load CAD (nominal, STEP/STL) → Load CT 3D image (actual) → Actual → surface mesh (choose a route: image segmentation → ROI → mesh, or sub-voxel Surface Determination, with a detailed comparison) → Registration (best-fit ICP) → Deviation map (signed nearest-surface distance, coloured by tolerance) → Results & Measurement Inspector (max/mean/RMS, % within tolerance, histogram). The core actions run in-process on numpy/skimage/trimesh; buttons also open Dragonfly's built-in Surface Determination / Mesh Registration / Measurement Inspector tools.\n\n**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the first tab runs the whole comparison unattended - reference, measured volume, surface, registration, deviation, statistics - each step with whatever its own tab shows when you press it. Four tick boxes, and the defaults follow one rule: a step that FABRICATES data is off, a step that MEASURES is on. Making a synthetic reference (OFF) would replace a CAD model loaded from file; making a synthetic CT volume (OFF) fabricates data and re-selects the Channel every later step measures. Extracting the surface (ON) is the first step of the measurement itself - untick it to re-use a surface you built by hand - and the deviation map (ON) is the workshop's result, which the statistics step reads. Every tab stays open at all times so the parameters can be read and changed BEFORE the run; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses at its own button and says which step is missing, instead of the tab being locked shut.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: learn CAD comparison / nominal-actual deviation analysis (first-article inspection, dimensional & GD&T checks, mould shrinkage/warp, additive-manufacturing QC, distortion/wear analysis); understand the difference between image segmentation and surface determination for extracting a surface from CT; run the deviation workflow on your own CAD (STEP/STL) + CT data.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no internet, no GPU, no venv — runs in-process on Dragonfly's own numpy/skimage/trimesh. Loading STEP files needs Dragonfly 2027.1+ (STL/OBJ/PLY work on all versions)."
