  "en": [
    {
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Nominal-Actual Comparison** is a hands-on industrial-CT metrology project that teaches and runs the core workflow — **CAD comparison / deviation analysis** — end to end: align a part's **actual** (CT scan) to its **nominal** (CAD design), compute the deviation everywhere, and judge conformance."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "This feature is provided by a third party (Prototype Labs / Apps), not officially developed or supported by Dragonfly. The completion certificate is also unofficial — for personal record only."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the first tab runs the whole comparison unattended - reference, measured volume, surface, registration, deviation, statistics - each step with whatever its own tab shows when you press it. Four tick boxes, and the defaults follow one rule: a step that FABRICATES data is off, a step that MEASURES is on. Making a synthetic reference (OFF) would replace a CAD model loaded from file; making a synthetic CT volume (OFF) fabricates data and re-selects the Channel every later step measures. Extracting the surface (ON) is the first step of the measurement itself - untick it to re-use a surface you built by hand - and the deviation map (ON) is the workshop's result, which the statistics step reads. Every tab stays open at all times so the parameters can be read and changed BEFORE the run; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses at its own button and says which step is missing, instead of the tab being locked shut."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The seven tabs",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "**Concepts** — nominal vs actual, the whole pipeline, typical applications.",
            "**Load CAD (Nominal)** — import a STEP/STL reference, or create a synthetic nominal part.",
            "**Load CT (Actual)** — pick a Channel as the scanned part, or create a synthetic CT with a known deviation.",
            "**Actual → surface mesh** — two routes: image segmentation → ROI → mesh; or sub-voxel Surface Determination (this tab compares them in detail).",
            "**Registration** — best-fit ICP overlays the actual mesh onto the nominal.",
            "**Deviation map** — signed nearest-surface distance, coloured by ± tolerance.",
            "**Results & Measurement Inspector** — max/mean/RMS, % within tolerance, histogram."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Segmentation vs Surface Determination (key)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Dimension",
              "Segmentation → mesh",
              "Surface Determination"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "Surface location",
                "voxel-level, pinned to grid (staircase)",
                "sub-voxel, on the true boundary between voxels"
              ],
              [
                "Accuracy",
                "~±0.5 voxel",
                "~±0.1 voxel or better"
              ],
              [
                "Threshold",
                "very sensitive (one global threshold)",
                "local-gradient adaptive, robust to beam hardening"
              ],
              [
                "Best for",
                "quick visualisation, needing a ROI",
                "dimensional metrology, tolerancing, nominal-actual"
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Prefer surface determination for metrology-grade comparison**; segmentation is enough if you only need a ROI or a quick shape."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "On 'Load CAD' click 'Create synthetic nominal part'; on 'Load CT' click 'Create synthetic CT scan' (or use your own STEP/STL + CT).",
            "On 'Actual → Mesh', mesh with both routes and compare accuracy.",
            "On 'Registration' click 'Best-fit align (ICP)' to align actual to nominal.",
            "On 'Deviation map' set the tolerance and click 'Compute deviation map' for a coloured mesh.",
            "On 'Results' read the statistics/histogram, or click 'Open Measurement Inspector'.",
            "Finish on the 'Certificate' tab by entering your name to generate a completion certificate."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Requirements",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "No install, no internet, no GPU, no venv. The core actions run in-process on Dragonfly's own numpy/skimage/trimesh; buttons also open the built-in Surface Determination / Mesh Registration / Measurement Inspector. **Loading STEP needs Dragonfly 2027.1+** (STL/OBJ/PLY work on all versions)."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Obsidian Vault of Help Documents",
  "cn": {
    "func": "该插件可以一键把您已安装的 Dragonfly 帮助文档转换成一个对 Obsidian 友好的知识库(vault)。它读取 Dragonfly 安装目录下的帮助文件(<DragonflyInstall>\\Help\\Content 中的 MadCap HTML),自动完成 HTML→Markdown 转换:每个帮助主题生成一篇带 YAML 前言(标题/分类/标签/来源)的笔记,内部链接转为 [[双向链接]],表格转为 Markdown 表格,提示/注意框转为 Obsidian callout,下拉块转为小标题,插图按内容哈希复制到 _attachments 并保留相对链接;随后自动生成分类索引(Home 与各分类 MOC)、写入 .obsidian 配置,并内置一个离线检索插件(Dragonfly Help Search)——您用自然语言提问,它用 BM25 算法给出最相关的帮助段落并可一键打开,全程无需联网、无需 API Key、无需下载模型。转换完全在 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 中进行(已包含 lxml),不装 venv、不联网。生成的知识库始终与您当前的 Dragonfly 版本一致,可在每次升级后重新生成。",
    "scenarios": "适用于希望像本地维基一样浏览、搜索 Dragonfly 帮助文档的场合:快速定位某个工具或工作流的说明、把帮助文档接入 Obsidian 的双向链接与图谱视图,或作为本地 RAG 检索语料来回答\"如何用 Cellpose 分割细胞\"这类问题。因为内容来自您自己安装的 Dragonfly,所以不需要随插件分发上百 MB 的文件。",
    "requirements": "无需 GPU、无需联网、无需 venv。第一次点击\"Convert & Build Vault(转换并建立知识库)\"约需 10–90 秒。打开知识库需要免费的 Obsidian 应用(obsidian.md);首次打开时 Obsidian 会询问是否信任该文件夹,请点击\"Trust author and enable plugins(信任并启用插件)\",内置检索插件才会加载。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "With one click this plugin converts your installed Dragonfly help into an Obsidian-friendly knowledge base (vault). It reads the help files in your Dragonfly install (the MadCap HTML under <DragonflyInstall>\\Help\\Content) and performs the HTML→Markdown conversion automatically: each help topic becomes a note with YAML frontmatter (title/category/tags/source), internal links become [[wikilinks]], tables become Markdown tables, note/tip boxes become Obsidian callouts, dropdowns become sub-headings, and illustrations are copied into _attachments (content-hashed) with their relative links preserved. It then generates category indexes (a Home note and one Map-of-Content per category), writes the .obsidian config, and bundles an offline retrieval plugin (Dragonfly Help Search): you ask a question in plain language and it ranks the most relevant help passages with BM25 and opens them with one click — no internet, API key, or model download. The whole conversion runs in Dragonfly's own Python (lxml is already bundled), with no venv and no internet. The vault always matches your installed Dragonfly version and can be rebuilt after each update.",
    "scenarios": "Useful whenever you want to browse and search the Dragonfly help like a local wiki: quickly find the description of a tool or workflow, plug the help docs into Obsidian's backlinks and graph view, or use it as a local RAG corpus to answer questions such as 'how do I segment cells with Cellpose'. Because the content comes from your own Dragonfly install, no hundreds-of-MB payload is shipped with the plugin.",
    "requirements": "No GPU, no internet, no venv. The first 'Convert & Build Vault' takes about 10–90 seconds. Opening the vault requires the free Obsidian app (obsidian.md); the first time, Obsidian asks whether to trust the folder — click 'Trust author and enable plugins' so the bundled search plugin loads."
  }
}

{
  "title": "Open3D Mesh Tools",
  "cn": {
    "func": "Open3D 网格工具可对 Dragonfly 场景中的任意表面网格执行专业的网格处理操作。选择一个网格，挑选操作——简化（减少三角形数量）、平滑、清理缺陷、填补孔洞、计算法线、由顶点重建表面，或用 ICP 配准将一个网格对齐到另一个网格——设置参数后点击运行。结果会作为新网格发布回场景，原始网格保持不变。",
    "scenarios": "适用于对由 CT 或显微数据提取的网格进行后处理：为仿真、3D 打印或加速渲染而精简巨大的分割网格；平滑并修复骨骼、孔隙、纤维或工业零件的粗糙表面；以及对同一物体的两次扫描进行配准（如前后对比或与基准件的计量比对）。",
    "requirements": "首次使用：在 Setup 选项卡点击\"Setup Environment\"（约几分钟，下载数百 MB，需联网）。仅用 CPU，无需 GPU。在 Dragonfly 2027.1（Python 3.14）上不能用 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 创建该环境：请安装 python.org 的 Python（3.12、3.13 或 3.14）并填入面板的 Base Python；Dragonfly 2025.1 无需另装 Python。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Open3D Mesh Tools applies professional mesh-processing operations to any surface mesh in your Dragonfly scene. Pick a mesh, choose an operation — simplify (reduce triangle count), smooth, clean up defects, fill holes, compute normals, reconstruct a surface from vertices, or align one mesh to another with ICP registration — set the parameters, and click Run. The result is published back into the scene as a new mesh, leaving the original untouched.",
    "scenarios": "Useful whenever meshes extracted from CT or microscopy data need post-processing: shrinking huge segmentation meshes for simulation, 3D printing, or faster rendering; smoothing and repairing noisy surfaces of bones, pores, fibers, or industrial parts; and aligning two scans of the same object (e.g. before/after comparison or metrology against a reference).",
    "requirements": "First use: click \"Setup Environment\" on the Setup tab (a few minutes, a few hundred MB download; needs internet). CPU only — no GPU required. On Dragonfly 2027.1 (Python 3.14) the bundled Python cannot build this environment: install a python.org Python (3.12, 3.13 or 3.14) and enter it in the panel's Base Python field; Dragonfly 2025.1 needs no separate Python."
  }
}

{
  "title": "OpenFiberSeg (Fiber Separation)",
  "cn": {
    "func": "把一个已分割好的二值 Fiber ROI 分离成逐根纤维的 MultiROI，采用 OpenFiberSeg 纤维追踪算法（分水岭找中心点 → 沿方向逐根追踪 → 体素归属 → 体积后处理）。这是一个完全独立的实现，和 Dragonfly 内置的 Open Fiber Segmentation 互不依赖。界面为向导式多标签页（Setup / Input / Parameters / Run）：Setup 建立独立 venv；Input 选 ROI、命名输出、可选中心线；Parameters 提供预设(Default/Thin/Thick/Dense)与红色的图像相关参数(纤维直径、最短长度、拼接距离、分水岭水位、凸缺陷距离)；Run 里可选 Fast(单轴，默认，约提速 3 倍)或 Full(三轴，最精确)，并可勾选输出中心线 MultiROI。计算在插件自己的 venv 里多核运行，结果作为分割对象(MultiROI)发布。算法为 MIT 许可(Facundo Sosa-Rey, 2021)。",
    "scenarios": "适用于短纤维增强复合材料等 CT 数据中，纤维已被二值分割成一整块 ROI，但需要拆成单根纤维以做取向、长度、数量等统计与可视化的场景；尤其是密集、接触、近平行纤维(骨架法难以分开)时，方向追踪能更好地分离。",
    "requirements": "需要一个已存在的二值 Fiber ROI。首次使用在 Setup 页创建独立 venv 并安装 numpy(<2)、scipy、scikit-image、opencv-python；安装时需联网，运行时不需要 GPU。在 Dragonfly 2027.1（Python 3.14）上不能用 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 创建该环境：请安装 python.org 的 Python（3.12）并填入面板的 Base Python；Dragonfly 2025.1 无需另装 Python。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Separates one already-segmented binary Fiber ROI into individual fibers (a MultiROI) using the OpenFiberSeg fiber-tracking algorithm (watershed center points -> orientation-guided per-fiber tracking -> voxel assignment -> volumetric post-processing). This is a fully independent reimplementation, unrelated to and independent from Dragonfly's built-in Open Fiber Segmentation. The UI is a wizard with tabs (Setup / Input / Parameters / Run): Setup builds an isolated venv; Input picks the ROI, names the output, and optionally the centerline; Parameters offers presets (Default/Thin/Thick/Dense) plus the RED image-dependent knobs (fiber diameter, min length, stitching distance, watershed water level, convexity defect); Run offers Fast (single axis, default, ~3x faster) or Full (all 3 axis permutations, most accurate) and an optional centerline MultiROI. Compute runs multi-core inside the plugin's own venv; the result is published as a segmentation object (MultiROI). Algorithm is MIT licensed (Facundo Sosa-Rey, 2021).",
    "scenarios": "For CT of short-fiber-reinforced composites (and similar) where the fibers are already binarised as one ROI but must be split into per-fiber labels for orientation, length and count statistics or visualization - especially dense, touching, near-parallel fibers that a skeleton method under-separates, where orientation tracking does better.",
    "requirements": "Requires an existing binary Fiber ROI. First use builds an isolated venv and installs numpy(<2), scipy, scikit-image and opencv-python; internet is needed for setup only. No GPU is required. On Dragonfly 2027.1 (Python 3.14) the bundled Python cannot build this environment: install a python.org Python (3.12) and enter it in the panel's Base Python field; Dragonfly 2025.1 needs no separate Python."
  }
}

{
  "title": "OpenFOAM CFD: Pore-Scale Flow Simulation",
  "cn": {
    "func": "使用开源 OpenFOAM 求解器，直接在您分割好的三维数据上运行孔隙尺度的计算流体动力学（CFD）模拟。选择一个定义固体/孔隙结构的 ROI、MultiROI 或 Channel，设置流动方向以及网格和求解器选项（也可以从内置的演示模型开始，如平行通道、球堆积或管束），插件即会对孔隙空间划分网格并求解稳态不可压缩层流。得到的速度场和压力场会作为 Channel 导入回场景中，并同时给出计算出的达西（Darcy）渗透率。",
    "scenarios": "非常适合基于显微 CT 数据的数字岩石物理和多孔介质研究——例如估算岩石、土壤、膜材料、过滤器、泡沫、电池电极或增材制造点阵结构的渗透率。凡是需要从分割图像（而非实物流动实验）获得流场和输运特性的材料科学或地球科学工作流程，都可以使用它。",
    "requirements": "一次性安装：需要带 WSL2 的 Windows，并双击导入随附的 OpenFOAM 计算环境镜像；仅用 CPU，无需 GPU。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Runs a pore-scale computational fluid dynamics (CFD) simulation directly on your segmented 3D data using the open-source OpenFOAM solver. Select a ROI, MultiROI, or Channel that defines the solid/pore structure, choose the flow direction and mesh/solver options (or start from a built-in demo phantom such as parallel channels, a sphere pack, or a tube bundle), and the plugin meshes the pore space and solves steady incompressible laminar flow. The resulting velocity and pressure fields are imported back into the scene as Channels, together with a computed Darcy permeability value.",
    "scenarios": "Ideal for digital rock physics and porous-media research on micro-CT data — estimating permeability of rocks, soils, membranes, filters, foams, battery electrodes, or additively manufactured lattices. Useful to any materials or geoscience workflow that needs flow fields and transport properties from a segmented image rather than a physical flow experiment.",
    "requirements": "One-time setup: Windows with WSL2 plus a double-click import of the bundled OpenFOAM compute image; CPU only, no GPU needed."
  }
}

{
  "title": "Optical Metallography 3D",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：把一叠**腐蚀后的金相光学显微照片**（连续切片）重建为三维晶粒与晶界结构。八个标签页就是工作流程的八个步骤，按顺序排列，每一步只有在上一步产生结果之后才会开放：选择通道 → 切片对齐（可选） → 匀光与降噪 → 提取暗色晶界网络 → 逐层分水岭分割晶粒 → 按重叠把各层连成三维晶粒 → 插值（可选：在层间插入形状插值的合成层以消除台阶感） → 测量并发布为 MultiROI。插值一步被**特意安排在测量之前**：使用它时，表格、CSV 以及发布出去的每一个对象都描述插值体，名称中也带有倍数；跳过它或丢弃它的结果，测量的就是切片被切出来时的原样。输入直接取自已经导入 Dragonfly 的 image channel，体素尺寸由通道读取，因此只要您已在 Dragonfly 中完成标定，所有长度都是微米。其中“切片对齐”只做整像素平移、不做插值，并明确提示：Dragonfly 自带功能完整的 Slice Registration（在数据集上右键打开），涉及旋转、变形或较大偏移时请用它。\n\n「数据源」页的**一键执行全部步骤（按当前设置）**会无人值守地跑完整个流程：加载 → 对齐 → 提交预处理与边界参数 → 晶粒分割 → 三维连接 → 发布，每一步都使用你按下按钮那一刻各自页签上显示的设置，因此可以按下之后离开，回来再看结果。插值与网格化默认**关闭**（它们最昂贵），对齐默认**开启**（与「对齐」页自身的自动应用一致）；三者都是按钮旁的复选框，被跳过的步骤会写进运行日志。所有页签始终可以打开和修改参数，正是为了能在运行**之前**逐页检查：某一步所需的输入尚不存在时，按下**它自己的按钮**会给出提示，说明缺的是哪一步。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：金相连续切片（逐层抛光＋腐蚀＋拍照）得到的三维晶粒结构；需要真正的三维晶粒体积、等效直径与 D10/D50/D90 分布，而不只是单层的平面统计；需要把晶粒作为 MultiROI、晶界作为 ROI 带入 Dragonfly 做后续可视化、配准或与其它数据对比；需要判断自己的切片间距是否足够小、能不能支撑三维重建。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需安装、联网、GPU、管理员权限或虚拟环境——进程内 PyQt6 加上 Dragonfly 自带的 numpy、scipy 与 scikit-image。本插件针对的是腐蚀金相照片（晶界是暗线、晶粒内部同色）；若图像是取向着色的 EBSD 图，请改用《三维 EBSD 重建》插件。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: reconstructs three-dimensional grains and grain boundaries from a stack of ETCHED optical micrographs (serial sections). Eight tabs are the eight steps of the workflow, in order, each opening only once the step before it has produced something: pick the channel, align the slices (optional), flatten and denoise, extract the dark boundary network, watershed each slice into grains, link the slices into 3-D grains by overlap, optionally interpolate (shape-based synthetic slices between the measured ones, which remove the stair step), then measure and publish as a MultiROI. The interpolation step sits BEFORE the measurement on purpose: when you use it, the table, the CSV and every published object describe the interpolated volume and carry the factor in their names; skip it, or discard its result, and the sections are measured exactly as they were cut. The input is an image already imported into Dragonfly and the voxel size is read from the channel, so every length is in micrometres once you have calibrated it there. The alignment step is a whole-pixel translation with no interpolation, and it says so: Dragonfly's own Slice Registration (right-click the dataset) is the full tool, and is what to use when the slices are rotated, distorted or badly out.\n\n**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the Source tab runs the whole workflow unattended - load, align, commit the preprocessing and boundary settings, segment the grains, link, publish - each step with whatever its own tab shows at the moment you press it, so a run that takes the best part of an hour can be started and left. Interpolation and meshing are OFF by default because they are the expensive ones, and alignment is ON because the Align tab's own auto-apply is; each is a tick box beside the button and a skipped step is written into the log. Every tab stays open at all times so that all of those parameters can be read and changed BEFORE the run: a step whose input does not exist yet refuses when you press ITS button and says which step is missing.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: a 3-D grain structure from metallographic serial sectioning (polish, etch, photograph, repeat); needing real three-dimensional grain volumes, equivalent diameters and a D10/D50/D90 distribution rather than per-slice planimetry; bringing the grains into Dragonfly as a MultiROI and the boundaries as an ROI for visualisation or comparison with other data; deciding whether your slice spacing is small enough to support a 3-D reconstruction at all.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no internet, no GPU, no admin rights and no virtual environment - in-process PyQt6 plus the numpy, scipy and scikit-image Dragonfly already ships. This plugin is for an etched micrograph, where boundaries are dark lines and the grain interiors are all the same; for an orientation-coloured EBSD map use 3D EBSD instead."
  }
}

{
