          "kind": "image",
          "file": "manual_images/en/01_source.png",
          "caption": "The Source tab. The channels, the slice range, and the memory and time the run will cost — printed before you commit to it."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**One channel** for a grey image, or for one band of a colour image."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Three channels** for a colour image Dragonfly split into Red / Green / Blue. They are paired **by name**: the first title whose leading word is 'Red', then the Green and Blue whose names match that same image. Pairing by position would join 'Green - Sample 2' to 'Red - Sample 1' whenever two colour images are open."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The three bands are combined with the standard luma weights. The **slice range** lets you work on part of the stack while tuning; the memory and the time it will cost are printed before you commit, because the reference stack is 207 million voxels."
        }
