        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Porosity Analysis (Hands-on Workshop)** is the first project in the **Hands-on Workshops** category: a **multi-tab teaching wizard** that walks you through the complete workflow of analysing the pore structure of **porous media** (digital rock, metal foams, filter media, bone, ...). A toolbar at the top (Overview, an Image dropdown, Refresh) sits above **five linked step tabs** that you work left to right."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "Every tab pairs two kinds of content: **📖 Learn** buttons open a resizable, **中文|EN**-switchable teaching pop-up that explains the concepts and workflow in depth; **🛠 Try it** buttons run the analysis on **real data**. Everything runs **in-process** on Dragonfly's bundled **numpy/scipy** — no venv, no download, no GPU, no internet."
        },
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the Import tab runs the whole workshop unattended - use the selected image, choose the threshold with Otsu, compute the total porosity, split open from closed porosity, count the pore clusters, estimate the permeability - each step with whatever its own tab shows at the moment you press it. Nothing is written to the session unless you tick one of the two boxes in that group (creating the synthetic sample publishes a Channel; creating the pore ROI publishes an ROI); both are off by default. Every tab stays open at all times, so an instructor can set every parameter BEFORE the run and a learner can still work the steps one at a time; a step whose input does not exist yet refuses when you press ITS button and says which step has to run first."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "Use it for teaching and self-study (couple abstract pore concepts with real operations, learning by doing); onboarding new staff/students to digital-rock analysis quickly; as a guided standard operating procedure that prevents skipping key steps (threshold checking, connectivity, REV, permeability estimate); and as an interactive tutorial for demos and marketing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The five steps & teaching content",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The five tabs are the five steps of pore analysis. Each carries 3 **📖 Learn** documents and one or more **🛠 Try it** actions:"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Step (tab)",
              "📖 Learn documents",
              "🛠 Try it actions"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "1 · Import",
                "3D imaging of porous media; voxel, resolution & representativeness; image formats & import",
                "Create synthetic porous sample; open Dragonfly import; use the selected image"
              ],
              [
                "2 · Segment",
                "Thresholding & Otsu; advanced segmentation methods; threshold pitfalls",
                "Auto threshold (Otsu) with porosity preview; create & publish a pore ROI"
              ],
              [
                "3 · Porosity",
                "Porosity definition & formula; open/closed porosity & connectivity; REV",
                "Compute total porosity; open vs closed connectivity analysis"
              ],
              [
                "4 · Pore Network",
                "The Pore Network Model (PNM); SNOW watershed extraction; network metrics",
                "Lightweight pore stats (connected components); guide to full SNOW extraction"
              ],
              [
                "5 · Simulation",
                "Darcy's law & permeability; simulation methods (PNM/LBM/Stokes); Kozeny–Carman",
                "Kozeny–Carman permeability estimate; guide to rigorous OpenPNM simulation"
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Features",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**One-click synthetic sample:** enter a sample size (voxels), target porosity φ and pore coarseness (blobiness) to generate a practice volume with a **known porosity** and publish it as a Channel. It prefers **porespy** (if present in the Dragonfly environment) and otherwise falls back to a **numpy Gaussian-random-field** generator — so you can start even with no data."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Otsu auto-threshold:** a pure-numpy Otsu (maximum between-class variance) finds the segmentation threshold and previews the porosity; tick **\"Pore = low intensity\"** (pores are usually dark in CT) and fine-tune the threshold manually."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Pore ROI segmentation & publishing:** build an **ROI** of the pore-phase voxels at the current threshold and publish it back into Dragonfly (`getAsROIWithinRange`) so you can check the boundary in 2D slices / 3D."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Porosity calculation:** φ = pore voxels / total voxels — a dimensionless ratio, independent of voxel size."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Open/closed connectivity analysis:** `scipy.ndimage.label` (26-connectivity) labels pore clusters, marks clusters touching a boundary face as **open** and fully-enclosed ones as **closed**, and reports total/open/closed porosity, cluster count, largest-cluster share and cluster-size distribution."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Kozeny–Carman permeability estimate:** from porosity φ and a mean grain size d, estimate k = φ³·d² / [180·(1−φ)²], converted to m² / Darcy / mD (order-of-magnitude)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Rich bilingual teaching docs:** 15 📖 Learn documents cover imaging physics, thresholding/segmentation, porosity, connectivity, REV, the pore network model, SNOW, Darcy's law, simulation methods and more — each **中文|EN**-switchable, resizable and left open while you work."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How to use",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "steps",
          "steps": [
            "Open **Prototype Apps ▸ Hands-on Workshops ▸ Porosity Analysis...** in Dragonfly.",
            "Click **📘 Overview** at the top first to read the workshop overview and see how the five steps connect.",
            "**Step 1 (Import):** with no data, set the sample size / target porosity / coarseness and click **🧪 Create synthetic porous sample** to generate and publish one; with your own data use **📂 Open Dragonfly import**, then come back, click **↻ Refresh** and pick it in the Image dropdown.",
            "**Step 2 (Segment):** click **🎯 Auto threshold (Otsu)** to find the threshold and preview porosity, adjust the Threshold manually if needed and confirm **Pore = low intensity**; then **🧩 Create pore ROI** and check the boundary hugs the real pore walls in slices / 3D.",
            "**Step 3 (Porosity):** click **📊 Compute total porosity** for φ; click **🔗 Open vs closed (connectivity)** to split open/closed pores and view cluster stats (only open porosity contributes to flow).",
            "**Step 4 (Pore Network):** click **🕸 Lightweight pore stats** for cluster count, open/closed fractions, largest-cluster share and size distribution; for a full pore-body/throat network, follow the prompt to the **ROI to MultiROI (SNOW)** plugin.",
            "**Step 5 (Simulation):** enter a mean grain size d and click **⚗ Estimate permeability (Kozeny–Carman)** for an order-of-magnitude k; for rigorous quantitative values, follow the prompt to the **Permeability (OpenPNM)** plugin.",
            "At any step, click that tab's **📖 Learn** buttons to study the concept, then return to **🛠 Try it** to verify hands-on."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Requirements",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**No venv, no download, no GPU, no admin, no internet.** All actions run in-process on Dragonfly's bundled **numpy/scipy**."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**The action buttons run inside Dragonfly** (they read Channels and publish ROIs via the object model). The teaching docs work anywhere — in a standalone test environment with no Dragonfly object model, 📖 Learn still works and 🛠 Try it reports that it must run inside Dragonfly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "**Synthetic-sample generation** prefers **porespy** (if installed in the Dragonfly environment) and otherwise falls back to a **numpy Gaussian-random-field** generator; neither path needs any extra install."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Tips & delegation",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "The pore-network and simulation steps here are deliberately **lightweight, in-process** approximations: Step 4 gives a connectivity snapshot via connected-component labelling, and Step 5 gives an **order-of-magnitude** permeability via Kozeny–Carman."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "For a full **pore-body/throat network extraction** (coordination number, pore/throat-size distributions), use the Prototype Apps **ROI to MultiROI (SNOW)** plugin (porespy's SNOW watershed algorithm)."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "For **rigorous permeability** (absolute permeability, two-phase drainage, relative-permeability curves), extract the network first then use the **Permeability (OpenPNM)** plugin. These heavier plugins may each need a one-time environment setup."
        },
        {
          "kind": "bullet",
          "text": "Key insight: permeability k ∝ φ³ — the **cube** of porosity! A small porosity change is amplified cubically, so always verify the segmentation threshold rather than blindly trusting the automatic value."
        },
        {
          "kind": "note",
          "text": "This is the first project in the Hands-on Workshops category; its multi-tab StepTab + bilingual DocDialog framework is reusable to build more hands-on workshops for other domains."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "title": "Prototype Apps Menu Manager",
  "cn": {
    "func": "把“显示/隐藏顶部 Prototype Apps 菜单”和“移除全部 Prototype Apps 菜单与插件”合并到一个插件里。核心是一个可配置动作（Configurable Action）“Toggle Prototype Apps menu”，默认快捷键 Left Ctrl + Left Shift + P：按一下即在运行时切换顶部 “Prototype Apps” 菜单的显示/隐藏（无需重启，下次启动会自动恢复）。因为 Dragonfly 的菜单栏是编译好的 C++、没有隐藏菜单的 Python 接口，所以本插件通过 Qt 找到主窗口菜单栏并翻转该菜单项的可见性。快捷键可在 Preferences ▸ Configurable Actions 里搜索 “Toggle Prototype Apps menu” 双击改成任意按键。插件还提供一个停靠面板（Prototype Apps ▸ Prototype Apps Menu Manager…）：顶部说明该快捷键并带“立即切换”按钮；下部是原“Remove All Menus & Plugins”工具——可“隐藏全部菜单（保留文件与环境，可逆）”或“彻底删除全部文件（插件/代码/商店/venv，不可逆，需勾选确认）”，只影响 Prototype Apps，不动 Prototype Labs 内核。",
    "scenarios": "适用于：想用一个键快速隐藏/恢复顶部 Prototype Apps 菜单（演示、录屏、界面精简）；或想一次性隐藏/彻底清除所有 Prototype Apps 组件。",
    "requirements": "在进程内运行，无需 venv、GPU 或联网。配置动作在 Dragonfly 重启后出现在 Preferences ▸ Configurable Actions；默认按键由安装器写入 preferences.xml（需在 Dragonfly 关闭时安装），也可自行在该界面绑定。移除功能依赖已安装的 Prototype Apps 中央商店。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Merges 'show/hide the top Prototype Apps menu' and 'remove all Prototype Apps menus & plugins' into one plugin. The core is a CONFIGURABLE ACTION 'Toggle Prototype Apps menu' (default Left Ctrl+Left Shift+P): one press toggles the top-level 'Prototype Apps' menu's visibility at runtime (no restart; it returns on next launch). Dragonfly's menu bar is compiled C++ with no Python hide API, so the plugin reaches the main window's menu bar through Qt and flips that menu action's visibility. Rebind the key any time in Preferences ▸ Configurable Actions → search 'Toggle Prototype Apps menu'. The plugin also provides a dockable panel (Prototype Apps ▸ Prototype Apps Menu Manager…): the top explains the shortcut with a 'Toggle now' button; the bottom is the former 'Remove All Menus & Plugins' tool — Hide all menus (keep files & environments, reversible) or permanently DELETE all files (plugins/code/store/venvs, irreversible, requires a confirmation). Affects ONLY Prototype Apps; the Prototype Labs core is untouched.",
    "scenarios": "For quickly hiding/restoring the top Prototype Apps menu with a keystroke (demos, screen recording, decluttering the UI), or for hiding / fully removing all Prototype Apps components at once.",
    "requirements": "Runs in-process; no venv, GPU or internet. The configurable action appears in Preferences ▸ Configurable Actions after a Dragonfly restart; the default key is written to preferences.xml by the installer (install with Dragonfly closed), or bind it yourself there. The removal feature needs the installed Prototype Apps central store."
  }
}

{
