  "en": {
    "func": "A dockable panel, inside Dragonfly, for training a deep-learning segmentation model on a REMOTE Dragonfly server. The top of the panel sets the remote server's address, port and access token; below it is the exact Remote DL Training tab from the standalone app (feed a Channel + MultiROI as ground truth, with optional validation split, visual feedback, a live loss curve, and save / download / import-to-local / apply-to-full-volume when done). Every request goes to the server you set at the top, so a GPU-less machine's Dragonfly can offload training to another GPU-equipped Dragonfly server (via a Tailscale IP such as 100.64.0.2 or a LAN IP such as 192.168.0.82). A remote connection requires the correct token; a 127.0.0.1 connection needs none.",
    "scenarios": "For offloading slow DL training from a local (GPU-less / limited) machine to a remote GPU server: prepare the training data in the client Dragonfly, submit it to the remote server with one click, and watch the loss curve + segmentation preview locally in real time.",
