  "en": [
    {"heading": "Introduction", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**From STL to Image** is a hands-on project — the **inverse** of 'From Image to STL: The Basics': it turns a surface-only STL mesh, step by step, back into a solid **3D binary image** (voxels). This process is called **voxelisation**."},
      {"kind": "p", "text": "**Execute All Steps with Current Settings** on the Concepts tab runs the six workflow steps unattended - use the selected mesh, create the bounding box, lay out the empty ROI, export the mesh surface into it, fill it to a solid and convert it to a binary image - each step with whatever its own tab shows at the moment you press it. It does NOT replace working through the tabs by hand: every step button and every Learn document stays exactly where it is. It is for the second pass, after you have changed the box type or the voxel spacing, and for an instructor demonstrating the finished pipeline in one press. The run publishes an ROI and the binary image; creating a sample STL first is a tick box, on only when your session holds no mesh at all. Every tab stays open at all times - a step whose input does not exist yet refuses at its own button and names the step that has to run first."},
      {"kind": "note", "text": "This feature is provided by a third party (Prototype Labs / Apps), not officially developed or supported by Dragonfly. The completion certificate is also unofficial — for personal record only."}
    ]},
    {"heading": "The whole pipeline (6 steps)", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "table", "table": {"headers": ["Step", "Input → Output", "In a nutshell"], "rows": [
        ["1. Import STL", ".stl → mesh", "read the surface in"],
        ["2. Bounding box", "mesh → Box", "frame the part, set the frame"],
        ["3. Empty ROI", "box + spacing → empty ROI", "lay an empty grid in the box"],
        ["4. Export Mesh to ROI", "mesh + empty ROI → shell ROI", "mark the surface into voxels"],
        ["5. Fill", "shell ROI → solid ROI", "fill the hollow interior"],
        ["6. To image", "solid ROI → binary image", "make a 0/1 volume"]
      ]}}
    ]},
    {"heading": "The two bounding boxes (key)", "blocks": [
      {"kind": "table", "table": {"headers": ["Dimension", "Minimal box (AABB)", "Oriented box (OBB)"], "rows": [
        ["Orientation", "aligned to world X/Y/Z", "rotated to hug the part's axes"],
        ["Tightness", "looser for tilted parts, wastes voxels", "tightest, fewest empty voxels"],
        ["Resulting image", "aligned to original axes, intuitive", "along the part's axes; looks straightened/rotated"],
