{
  "title": "Synthetic RVE Builder",
  "cn": {
    "func": "生成人工的三维微观结构，用于仿真输入、方法验证或补充训练数据。两条路径：参数化生成，什么都不需要先发布，结构由参数凭空造出；以及样本约束合成，由一张二维切片的统计量约束三维结构。四类参数化生成器：椭球（任意三维取向，可自由重叠，也可硬核不重叠或带间隙）、纤维（直的或蠕虫状链）、管网（带喉道半径分布的连通网络，并在栅格上实测是否贯通）、粗糙表面（给定 Hurst 指数与均方根粗糙度的自仿射表面，含 Brown 失配波长裂缝隙宽）。样本约束合成先测出样本的两点相关函数与体积分数，反演出其背后高斯场的相关函数，用谱方法生成三维场，再按体积分数精确取阈。两处刻意不粉饰：一张二维样本只有在介质沿第三方向统计各向同性时才能约束三维结构，因此插件会测量样本自身的各向异性，对层状或纤维状材料给出醒目告警——建立在错误假设上、看似合理的结构，比没有结构更糟；当要求的相关函数物理上不可实现时，被截断的谱能量会被报告出来，而不是悄悄吸收。六个编号步骤：选择模式（参数化无需输入，样本模式需要一张切片）；设定体素尺寸、原点与二值化方式；按生成器种类填参数；在小体积上预览，显示实际达到的体积分数与相关函数对照（不发布任何对象）；全尺寸运行；最后发布为 Channel 或 MultiROI，并导出表格、单文件 HTML 与完整来源记录。 另有一个不编号的「分享报告」标签页：通过 Cloudflare 临时快速隧道，把已生成的单文件 HTML 报告直接从本机发布出去，不上传、也不需要账号；该地址是公开的、没有密码（拿到链接的任何人都能读，而页面本身就带着您的图像数据），隧道建立后大约还要 40 秒它才开始响应，停止分享或关闭窗口后即永久失效。",
    "scenarios": "适用于：为有限元或格子玻尔兹曼仿真造一个统计特征受控的输入结构；在已知答案的合成结构上验证一条测量流程；由少量真实二维切片扩充三维训练数据；以及研究某个参数（孔隙率、纤维长径比、喉道半径分布）如何影响下游计算结果。",
    "requirements": "无需任何安装或配置：完全运行在 Dragonfly 自带的 Python 中，使用其已附带的 NumPy 与 SciPy。不联网、不下载、不需要 GPU、不创建虚拟环境。 唯一的例外是可选的「分享报告」标签页：它需要本机能访问外网，并会在您确认后一次性下载 Cloudflare 的 cloudflared.exe（约 52 MB，按用户保存）。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "Generates artificial 3-D microstructures for simulation input, method validation or data augmentation. Two routes: parametric generation, which needs nothing published because the structure is invented from the parameters; and exemplar-constrained synthesis, where a single 2-D slice constrains the statistics of a 3-D volume. Four parametric families: ellipsoids at any 3-D orientation, freely interpenetrating or hard-core with an optional clearance; fibres as straight or wormlike chains; tube networks, a connected graph with a throat-radius distribution whose percolation is measured on the raster rather than assumed; and rough surfaces, self-affine at a given Hurst exponent and RMS roughness, including Brown mismatched-wavelength fracture apertures. The exemplar route measures the slice's two-point correlation and volume fraction, inverts them to the correlation of the underlying Gaussian field, synthesises that field spectrally, and thresholds it at the level that reproduces the volume fraction exactly. Two places it deliberately does not flatter the user: a 2-D exemplar can only constrain a 3-D volume if the medium is statistically isotropic in the third direction, so the plugin measures the exemplar's own anisotropy and warns prominently for a layered or fibrous material — a plausible-looking structure built on a broken assumption is worse than none — and where the requested correlation is not physically realisable, the clipped spectral energy is reported rather than silently absorbed. Six numbered steps: choose the mode (parametric needs no input, the exemplar mode needs one slice); set the voxel size, origin and how the exemplar is binarised; fill in the parameters for the chosen generator; preview on a small volume showing the achieved volume fraction and the correlation overlay, publishing nothing; run at full size; and finally publish as a Channel or a MultiROI and export the tables, the self-contained HTML and the complete provenance record. An unnumbered Share Report tab puts the finished one-file HTML report on the internet temporarily through a Cloudflare quick tunnel, served straight from this machine with no upload and no account: the address is public and has no password (anyone with the link can read it, and the page carries your image data itself), it only starts answering roughly 40 s AFTER the tunnel is started, and it stops working permanently once sharing is stopped or the window is closed.",
    "scenarios": "Use it to build a simulation input whose statistics you control, for finite-element or lattice-Boltzmann work; to validate a measurement pipeline on a structure whose answer is known in advance; to augment 3-D training data from a handful of real 2-D slices; and to study how one parameter — porosity, fibre aspect ratio, throat-radius spread — propagates into a downstream calculation.",
    "requirements": "Nothing to install or configure: it runs entirely in Dragonfly's own Python using the NumPy and SciPy it already ships. No internet, no download, no GPU, no virtual environment. The one exception is the optional Share Report tab: it needs outbound internet access and downloads Cloudflare's cloudflared.exe once (about 52 MB, kept per user) with your confirmation."
  }
}

{
