    {
      "heading": "The automatic voxel size, and why it matters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "p",
          "text": "The voxel size is chosen from the **vessel radius**, not from the bounding box: automatic = local vessel radius / 8 voxels per radius, with the radius estimated as 2V/A (for a long tube V = pi r^2 L and A = 2 pi r L, so 2V/A is the radius and no centerline is needed)."
