          "text": "This is load-bearing. Below about two voxels per radius the voxelised tube short-circuits its own bends and the skeleton runs through solid that does not exist in the mesh. Measured on two real specimens that differ only in calibre: at **1.39** voxels per radius, **45 of 175** centerline samples ended up **outside** the mesh; at **3.02**, none did. Finer is slower but loses fewer samples, and the panel says so."
