          "text": "A sample that is outside the mesh is reported as **missing**, never as a small positive radius — the distance to a surface is unsigned, so a point that has drifted outside would otherwise return a perfectly plausible radius. Where a contiguous stretch is lost, it is bridged by interpolating between the two measured samples that bound it and then recentred onto the cross-section; the report states how many samples were **bridged**, how many are **still outside**, and how many cross-sections were **excluded**."
