{
  "title": "In-range fraction in the current view (live)",
  "cn": {
    "func": "功能：实时显示当前 2D 视图中有多大比例的体素落在 ROI Tools 的「**Define range**」（也就是那片红色预览）范围内。范围的上下限和开关状态是**从对象模型里直接读取**的（`VisualChannel.getRangeSelectionEnabledForView` 与 `get2DWindowLevel2Min/MaxForView` —— 与 Dragonfly 自己在视图上显示「Selection Min/Max」所用的是同样几个访问器），**不需要你把范围再手输一遍**：在 ROI Tools 里勾上 Define range，在本面板点「开始」，随后滚动切片、缩放、平移时数字都会跟着更新。结果**永远同时给出两个占比，并各自写明分母**：「**可见视口**」= 视图矩形中确实承载图像数据的像素（按**屏幕像素网格**统计），以及「**整张当前切片**」= 视图下方那一张切片的全部体素（按**数据体素间距**统计）。每个百分比旁边都列出计数（例如 `800 / 1,600`），因为空视图或被裁掉的视图必须能被看出来，而不是被一个 `0.00%` 藏起来。同样的文字会以 `VisualText` 画在视图上（可关闭，关闭面板时自动移除）。另有两种模式：**手动范围**（读数里会明确写着「在此输入，并非读取 ROI Tools」），以及**所选 ROI 的面积占比**（同样按上述两个区域统计）。凡是无法诚实测量的情况都**只给理由、不给数字**：3D 视图或非平面 2D 视图、Define range 没开、或视图中有多于一个数据集开着范围（这种歧义 Dragonfly 自己也拒绝猜）。本插件只读取，不创建、不修改任何 Dragonfly 对象。【读数的外观】「**结果**」分组最上方只用大字给出**一个**数字：**可见视口**中被标记的体素占比，旁边直接写明它是谁的比例；面板里每一个颜色都从 Dragonfly 自身主题推导并对背景实测对比度 —— 因为首版写死了一个深藏青，在深色主题上只有 1.03:1，确实看不清。同一个数字也会画到视图上，默认在**右侧**、用**橘黄色**（`#FF9F1C`，可用取色器修改）显示，字号是 Dragonfly 自身标注字号的倍数；默认只把可见视口的数字画到画面上，整张切片的数字留在面板里。视图上的读数尚未在实际会话中确认能渲染出来，面板也如实声明了这一点。",
    "scenarios": "适用场景：一边拖动 Define range 的阈值、一边看着阈值选中的体素占当前视图的比例，用来快速定阈值；比较同一套数据在不同切片位置上的占比；放大到某个感兴趣区域后，读「可见视口」那一行来只统计眼前这一块；把某个已有 ROI 的面积占比按切片读出来（不必先做测量表）；给同事或客户演示时，把这个占比直接显示在视图上截图。",
    "requirements": "环境需求：无需安装、联网、GPU、管理员权限或虚拟环境 —— 纯进程内 PyQt6，加上 Dragonfly 自带的 numpy。要求当前视图是**平面 2D 视图**，并且视图中有可见的数据集；若要用 Define range 模式，还需要在 ROI Tools 面板里勾上「Define range」。**永远不会整卷读取**：每次更新只按当前平面重采样一张切片（`getSliceIntersectingBoundedPlane`），对约 100 万像素的切片，计数约 2 毫秒；面板会把**实测的每次更新耗时**、更新次数与空转心跳次数一起显示出来，所以在超大数据上变慢时你能看见原因，而不用猜。更新间隔可调（100–5000 毫秒，默认 250），并可设「抽样步长」用精度换速度 —— 一旦步长大于 1，读数会写明这是抽样估计。范围上下限按**物理单位**读取后再用 `(值 − offset) / slope` 换算成体素原始值参与比较，所以在有标定（slope/offset 非 1/0）的数据上同样正确。"
  },
  "en": {
    "func": "What it does: shows LIVE what proportion of the current 2D view lies inside the ROI Tools \"**Define range**\" -- the red preview. The bounds and the on/off state are **read straight out of the object model** (`VisualChannel.getRangeSelectionEnabledForView` plus `get2DWindowLevel2Min/MaxForView`, the same accessors Dragonfly's own on-canvas \"Selection Min/Max\" readout uses), so **you never retype the range**: tick Define range in ROI Tools, press Start here, and the number follows you as you scroll, zoom and pan. **Two fractions are always reported and each states its own denominator**: the **visible viewport** = the pixels of the view rectangle that actually carry image data, counted on the **screen-pixel grid**; and the **whole current slice** = every voxel of the slice under the view, at the **data spacing**. Every percentage carries its counts beside it (`800 / 1,600`), because an empty or clipped view has to be visible rather than hidden behind `0.00%`. The same text is painted on the view as a `VisualText` readout, which can be switched off and is removed when the panel closes. Two further modes: a **manual range**, which says in the readout itself that it was typed here and is NOT the tool's range; and the **selected ROI's area fraction** over the same two regions. Anything that cannot be measured honestly is refused with a reason and NO number: a 3D or non-planar 2D view, Define range switched off, or more than one visible dataset with a range on (an ambiguity Dragonfly itself declines to resolve). The plugin only reads: it creates and modifies nothing. The **Result** panel leads with ONE big number -- the percentage of the **visible viewport** that is marked, with what it is a percentage of spelled out beside it -- and every colour in the panel is derived from Dragonfly's own theme and measured against its background, because the first release hardcoded a navy that was 1.03:1 on the dark theme and genuinely unreadable. The same figure is painted on the view, by default on the **right-hand side** in **orange** (`#FF9F1C`, settable with a colour picker), at a text size that is a multiple of Dragonfly's own annotation font; only the visible-viewport figure goes on the canvas, and the whole-slice figure stays in the panel. The on-view readout has not yet been confirmed to render in a live session, and the panel says so.",
    "scenarios": "Typical scenarios: choosing a threshold by dragging the Define-range handles while watching what proportion of the view they select; comparing that proportion between slice positions in the same dataset; zooming into a region of interest and reading the \"visible viewport\" line so only what is on screen is counted; reading an existing ROI's area fraction slice by slice without first building a measurement table; and putting the figure on the view itself for a screenshot when showing results to a colleague or a customer.",
    "requirements": "Requirements: no install, no internet, no GPU, no admin, no venv -- pure in-process PyQt6 plus the numpy Dragonfly already ships. The current view must be a **planar 2D view** with a visible dataset in it; the Define-range mode additionally needs \"Define range\" ticked in the ROI Tools panel. **The volume is never read whole**: each update resamples ONE slice on the current plane (`getSliceIntersectingBoundedPlane`), about 2 ms of counting for a ~1 megapixel slice. The panel prints its **measured per-update cost**, the update count and the number of idle heartbeats, so on a very large dataset you can see why a short interval is expensive instead of guessing. The interval is settable (100-5000 ms, default 250) and a \"Subsample stride\" trades exactness for speed -- above 1 the readout says the number is a sampled estimate. The range bounds are read in **physical units** and converted to raw voxel values with `(value - offset) / slope` before any comparison, so the answer is also correct on calibrated data where slope/offset are not 1/0."
  }
}

